md`# brain-core

The Worker every other Worker is bound to. It routes a method or a path to the Worker of the service that declared it, and keeps what must last: the notebook-side rows, the route table and the rules the owner sets.

It answers bindings only. A caller is who the kernel says it is, and the kernel is known by its key; any other Worker is \`worker:NAME\`, whatever it claims.

| answer | when |
|---|---|
| 403 \`Forbidden\` | A Worker calls a method that its service did not declare in \`calls\` (mode \`enforce\`). A member's Worker calls outside its author's reach, or is switched off. A rule cannot be decided. |
| 405 \`InvalidRequest\` | A query sent as POST, or a procedure sent as GET. |
| 401 \`AuthRequired\` | The rule of the method or path is not true for this caller. |
| 429 \`RateLimitExceeded\` | A member's calls for the day are used. |
| 402 \`OutOfCredits\` | The method has a price and the account that pays has less than the price left for the day, or the call has no account. |
| 402 \`PriceOverCeiling\` | The price of this call is more than one call may cost. |
| 501 \`MethodNotImplemented\` | No service declares the method. |
| 502 \`UpstreamUnavailable\` | The Worker of the service that declares it is not bound to the core. |

| method | |
|---|---|
| \`rule.list\` | query, owner. The rules the owner set. |
| \`rule.put\`, \`rule.delete\` | procedure, the owner's own session. \`{ name, allow }\`: a CEL expression in place of the rule a service declared. A rule the service fixed is refused. |
| \`calls.list\` | query, owner. \`{ mode, implicit, undeclared: [{ worker, method, n }] }\`. |
| \`calls.setMode\` | procedure, the owner's own session. \`{ mode: "report" | "enforce" | null, clear }\`. |
| \`price.list\` | query, owner. \`{ prices: [{ target, worker, declared, set, setAt }], unit, defaults }\`. |
| \`price.put\`, \`price.delete\` | procedure, the owner's own session. \`{ target, price }\`: a CEL expression in place of the price a service declared. |
| \`quota.get\` | query, any account. \`{ who, day, spent, daily, remaining, resetsAt }\` for the caller's own account. The owner reads another with \`?who=\`. |
| \`quota.list\`, \`quota.ledger\` | query, owner. Each account's day, and the charges of one day (\`?day=&who=&limit=\`) with totals by account and by method. |
| \`quota.put\`, \`quota.setDefaults\` | procedure, the owner's own session. \`{ who, daily }\`, and \`{ owner, member, worker, token, perCall, keepDays }\`. \`null\` is the default again. |

**Origin.** A rule reads \`caller\`, who made the call, and \`origin\`, who started the chain of calls it is part of. The two have the same fields. For a call from outside they are equal. When a Worker makes a call while it answers one, \`caller\` is the Worker and \`origin\` is the origin of the call it answers. A call a Worker makes by its own schedule has the Worker as \`origin\`. For a member's Worker \`caller\` is its author, and so is \`origin\` when it answers nobody.

\`\`\`js
app.post(NS + "publish", async (c) => xrpc.procedure("com.lopecode.brain.bluesky.putRecord", record))
// the rule of bluesky.putRecord
'caller.session || (caller.worker == "brain-x-feed" && origin.kind == "owner")'
\`\`\`

The core sends a reference with each call it forwards (\`x-brain-context\`): the origin, the Worker it is for and an end time 120 s later, signed with HMAC-SHA-256 under a key that is one of the core's rows. The Worker wrapper (\`workerRuntime\` in \`@tomlarkworthy/cloudflare-iac\`) holds it while the Worker answers that call and sends it back with each call the Worker makes to the core in that time: \`xrpc\`, \`secrets\`, \`sql\`, \`inbox\`. On Cloudflare it is held in \`AsyncLocalStorage\`, so two calls answered at once keep their own. Until 2026-10-07 a service passed it on by hand (\`behalf\`, removed). The core reads a reference only from a Worker known by its key, and only one made for that Worker and not ended. Any other reference is ignored and the origin is the Worker. A Worker can use a reference again until it ends. The core also sends \`x-brain-origin\` and \`x-brain-origin-via\` in clear, for a Worker that decides rules of its own.

A rule that does not name \`origin\` lets the Worker act for anyone it answers. \`origin.trusted\` is true for the owner, a token, and an account the kernel passed for the first method of the chain. A rule of a secret or a table reads the same \`origin\`. A Worker holds a secret's value for 5 s for one origin, and asks again for another.

| call | rule reads origin | why |
|---|---|---|
| feed → \`bluesky.putRecord\`, \`bluesky.deleteRecord\` | yes | the record is public |
| inbox → \`*.send\` | no | the reply goes only to the address the entry came from |
| library → \`static.put\`, \`static.get\`, \`static.delete\` | no | the library decides who reads a notebook |
| whatsapp → \`static.put\` | no | a picture that arrived, with no caller |
| bluesky, whatsapp → \`lease.get\`, \`inbox.append\` | no | started by the Worker's own clock |
| any → \`secret.get\`, \`db.sql\` | no | the Worker's own secrets and tables |
| core → \`metrics.record\` | no | the core's own counts |

**Prices and credits** (added 2026-10-08). A method or a path can have a price beside its rule: a CEL expression over the same \`caller\`, \`origin\` and \`request\`, which gives US dollars. The owner's price (\`price.put\`) stands in for the declared one. A call with no price, or a price of 0, reads the route table and the settings the core already holds and writes no row.

\`\`\`js
"com.lopecode.brain.browser.extend": { type: "procedure", who: "owner", price: "double(request.params.seconds) * 0.000025" }
\`\`\`

The order is rule, price, charge, forward. The price is for the Worker's own work: a method it calls is charged by its own price when the call reaches the core. A price that throws, is not a number, or is less than 0 refuses the call with 403; one above \`perCall\` refuses it with 402. A price reads the query of the request and not its body, as a rule does.

| the call is started by | the account that pays | default a day |
|---|---|---|
| the owner's session, the owner's turn, the owner's PDS | \`owner\` | $1.00 |
| a member's session, PDS, portal or turn | \`did:…\`, the member | $0.10 |
| a turn in a room | the person who wrote the message, as any turn | |
| a token | \`token:NAME\` | $0.10 |
| a Worker by its own clock | \`worker:NAME\` | $0.10 |
| a member's Worker by its own clock | its author | |
| nobody (\`anonymous\`) | none: a priced call is refused | |

A Worker that answers a call spends the credits of that call's origin, through any number of Workers. The most one call may cost is $1. An account's day starts at 00:00 UTC.

A charge is taken before the call is forwarded and given back when the answer is not 2xx or the Worker throws. A Worker may answer \`x-brain-cost: <usd>\` to say the call cost less, and the core gives back the difference; a higher value, or one that is not an amount, is logged and not read. The answer to a priced call carries \`x-brain-price\`, what was charged in the end.

An account's day is one row, \`spend/DAY/ACCOUNT\`: a list that each charge and each amount given back is appended to in one statement. A charge counts when the charges that count before it, and it, are inside the allowance it was made under. The list alone decides that, so calls made at once do not spend past the allowance and no call holds a lock. A charge that lost to another made at the same time stays in the list and counts for nothing. A priced call is two statements (append, read) and one more when something is given back. A day holds 2000 charges for one account; the next is refused. A core that read an account as spent refuses it for 5 s without a write. Days older than \`keepDays\` (30) are deleted.

Limits. A cost known only after the call, such as the tokens of a model call, has no method yet: the price would have to be the most the call can cost, with \`x-brain-cost\` to bring it down. The allowance of a member's calls for a day (429) is a separate count.

**Calls.** A Worker calls the methods its service lists in \`calls\`. The core reads the list from the Worker's \`getInfo\`, which the deployer bound at deploy, and keeps it for that deployed hash. A name is exact. \`*\` is one part of a name; as the last part it is one or more: \`com.lopecode.brain.static.*\`, \`com.lopecode.brain.*.send\`. A list of only \`*\` matches nothing.

Three methods are not listed, because a platform cell calls them: \`secret.get\` (\`secrets\`), \`db.sql\` (\`sql\`) and \`inbox.append\` (\`inbox\`). Each has its own rule.

The kernel and the deployer are not checked: they are not Workers of a service. A member's Worker is not checked against a list either. The deployer writes \`calls: []\` for it, and each of its calls is checked as its author (see Members).

In mode \`report\` an undeclared call is counted and passed. In mode \`enforce\` it is refused. The default in the code is \`report\`; a Brain is in \`enforce\` after the owner sets it. At most 200 names are counted.`
// %%
core_service = cloudflare.Service("core", coreApp, { role: "core" })
// %%
// Announced to the page, so the Services list shows it. A cell of its own: a deployed function cannot depend on it.
core_announce = {
  plugins.add("workers", core_service, { invalidation });
  return "announced core_service";
}
// %%
coreApp = {
  const app = new hono.Hono();
  const NS = "/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.";
  const fail = (c, status, error, message) => c.json({ error, message }, status);
  const keys = new Map();
  // What the core forwards to: recipes, and system Workers such as the database.
  const routed = (r) => r.role === "recipe" || r.role === "system" || r.role === "member";
  const identify = async (request) => {
    const url = new URL(request.url);
    // From the internet only the deployer gets this far, and the wrapper has named it.
    if (!url.hostname.endsWith(".internal")) return { caller: ["deployer", "guard"].includes(request.headers.get("x-brain-caller")) ? "deployer" : "anonymous" }; // "guard": a wrapper from before 2026-10-08
    const key = request.headers.get("x-brain-key");
    if (!key) return { caller: "anonymous" };
    const hash = await sha256(key);
    if (!keys.has(hash)) {
      const known = await rows.get("key/" + hash);
      if (known) keys.set(hash, known);
    }
    const known = keys.get(hash);
    if (!known) return { caller: "anonymous" };
    // A member's Worker is known by its key like any other, and is then checked as its author.
    if (known.role === "member") return { caller: "worker:" + known.worker, keyed: known.worker, member: { worker: known.worker, author: known.author } };
    if (known.role !== "kernel") return { caller: "worker:" + known.worker, keyed: known.worker };
    return { caller: request.headers.get("x-brain-caller") || "anonymous", via: request.headers.get("x-brain-via") || "" };
  };
  // Origin. The caller of a call is who made it; the origin is who started the chain of calls it is part of. With
  // each call the core forwards goes a reference: the origin, the Worker it is for and when it ends, signed with a
  // key only the core holds (HMAC-SHA-256; the key is one of the core's own rows, made at first use). A Worker that
  // sends the reference back on a call it makes is given that origin. A reference that is absent, changed, ended or
  // made for another Worker gives nothing, and the origin is then the Worker itself. Nothing a Worker says in clear
  // is read. Signed and not kept: the core has many instances and none of them remembers a call.
  const CONTEXT_MS = 120000;
  const utf8 = new TextEncoder();
  const b64u = (bytes) => btoa(String.fromCharCode(...new Uint8Array(bytes))).replace(/\+/g, "-").replace(/\//g, "_").replace(/=+$/, "");
  const unb64u = (text) => Uint8Array.from(atob(text.replace(/-/g, "+").replace(/_/g, "/")), (ch) => ch.charCodeAt(0));
  let originKey = null;
  const keyOfOrigin = () =>
    (originKey ??= (async () => {
      if (!(await rows.get("origin-key"))) await rows.putIfAbsent("origin-key", b64u(crypto.getRandomValues(new Uint8Array(32))));
      return crypto.subtle.importKey("raw", utf8.encode(await rows.get("origin-key")), { name: "HMAC", hash: "SHA-256" }, false, ["sign", "verify"]);
    })().catch((e) => {
      originKey = null;
      throw e;
    }));
  const contextFor = async (worker, origin) => {
    const payload = b64u(utf8.encode(JSON.stringify({ o: origin.caller, v: origin.via || "", w: worker, e: Date.now() + (config.contextMs ?? CONTEXT_MS) })));
    return "c1." + payload + "." + b64u(await crypto.subtle.sign("HMAC", await keyOfOrigin(), utf8.encode(payload)));
  };
  const originFrom = async (reference, worker) => {
    const m = /^c1\.([A-Za-z0-9_-]+)\.([A-Za-z0-9_-]+)$/.exec(reference || "");
    if (!m) return null;
    try {
      if (!(await crypto.subtle.verify("HMAC", await keyOfOrigin(), unb64u(m[2]), utf8.encode(m[1])))) return null;
      const p = JSON.parse(new TextDecoder().decode(unb64u(m[1])));
      return p.w === worker && p.e > Date.now() && typeof p.o === "string" ? { caller: p.o, via: p.v || "" } : null;
    } catch {
      return null;
    }
  };
  // Every call the core answers or forwards is counted here. The counts are handed, in batches, to whichever
  // Worker whose service declares metrics.record; with none they are dropped. A fault (500 and above, except 501) is sent at once, the rest every 10 s.
  const RECORD = "com.lopecode.brain.metrics.record";
  const tele = { from: 0, buckets: new Map(), errors: [], route: null, routeAt: 0 };
  const flush = async () => {
    const batch = {
      from: tele.from,
      to: Date.now(),
      buckets: [...tele.buckets].map(([k, v]) => {
        const [worker, version, method, caller, status] = k.split("|");
        return { worker, version, method, caller, status: Number(status), ...v };
      }),
      errors: tele.errors
    };
    Object.assign(tele, { from: 0, buckets: new Map(), errors: [] });
    if (Date.now() - tele.routeAt >= (config.metricsRouteMs ?? 60000)) {
      tele.route = (await settings.list("route/")).map((r) => r.value).find((r) => r.methods && r.methods[RECORD]) || null;
      tele.routeAt = Date.now();
    }
    const short = tele.route && tele.route.worker.replace(/^brain-(x-)?/, "");
    if (!short || !workers.has(short)) return;
    await workers.fetch(short, new Request(`https://${short}.internal/xrpc/${RECORD}`, { method: "POST", headers: { "content-type": "application/json", "x-brain-caller": "worker:brain-core" }, body: JSON.stringify(batch) }));
  };
  const observe = async (c, started) => {
    const url = new URL(c.req.url), target = c.get("target"), status = c.res.status, ms = Date.now() - started;
    const nsid = url.pathname.startsWith(NS) ? url.pathname.slice(NS.length) : null;
    if (nsid && nsid.startsWith("metrics.")) return;
    // Names nobody declared are counted as one, so a stranger cannot grow the table.
    const method = !target && [404, 501].includes(status) ? "(unknown)" : nsid || c.get("path") || url.pathname;
    const who = c.get("who").caller, caller = /^(token|did):/.test(who) ? who.split(":")[0] : who;
    // The version that answered: the forwarded Worker's own header, or this core's.
    const by = (c.res.headers.get("x-brain-served-by") || "").split(",")[0].trim();
    const version = target ? (by.startsWith(target + "@") ? by.slice(target.length + 1) : "") : String((c.env && c.env.BRAIN_INFO && c.env.BRAIN_INFO.hash) || "").slice(0, 12);
    const key = [target || "brain-core", version, method, caller, status].join("|");
    const b = tele.buckets.get(key) || { n: 0, ms: 0, max: 0 };
    tele.buckets.set(key, { n: b.n + 1, ms: b.ms + ms, max: Math.max(b.max, ms) });
    // 501 is the answer to a name nobody declares: the caller's mistake, not a fault.
    if (status >= 500 && status !== 501) tele.errors.push({ t: started, worker: target || "brain-core", version, method, caller, status, ms });
    if (!tele.from) tele.from = started;
    if (tele.errors.length || Date.now() - tele.from >= (config.metricsFlushMs ?? 10000)) await flush();
  };
  // Members. The kernel hands over who is a member and what each was granted (people.sync), because a Worker
  // cannot ask the kernel. A member's Worker has its author's permissions and no others: a call it makes is
  // allowed when its author is still a member and the method is one of WORKER, a member's own method
  // (com.lopecode.brain.m.…), or in the author's grant. It then goes on as a call by that DID, with the Worker in
  // x-brain-via, so every rule and every store downstream sees the author.
  const WORKER = ["db.sql", "static.put", "static.get", "static.list", "static.tag", "static.setPublic", "static.delete", "blob.upload", "blob.get", "blob.info", "blob.list", "blob.tag", "blob.delete"].map((m) => "com.lopecode.brain." + m);
  const MEMBER_NS = "com.lopecode.brain.m.";
  const QUOTA = { calls: 2000, bytes: 20 * 1024 * 1024, workers: 3 };
  const quotaOf = (person) => ({ ...QUOTA, ...((person && person.quota) || {}) });
  const today = () => new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10);
  // Calls into and out of one member's Workers, counted per UTC day.
  const spend = async (person) => (await rows.increment(`mcalls/${person.did}/${today()}`)) <= quotaOf(person).calls;
  const asAuthor = async (c, { worker, author }) => {
    const url = new URL(c.req.url);
    const nsid = url.pathname.startsWith("/xrpc/") ? url.pathname.slice("/xrpc/".length) : null;
    const person = await rows.get("person/" + author);
    if (!person) return fail(c, 403, "Forbidden", `${author} is not a member, so ${worker} may call nothing`);
    const route = await rows.get("route/" + worker);
    if (!route || route.off) return fail(c, 403, "Forbidden", `${worker} is switched off`);
    if (!nsid || !(WORKER.includes(nsid) || nsid.startsWith(MEMBER_NS) || person.methods.includes(nsid))) return fail(c, 403, "Forbidden", `${worker} runs as ${author}, who has no grant for ${nsid || url.pathname}`);
    if (!(await spend(person))) return fail(c, 429, "RateLimitExceeded", `${author} has used today's ${quotaOf(person).calls} calls`);
    c.set("who", { caller: author, via: "worker:" + worker });
    return null;
  };
  // A Worker calls what its service declared in `calls`, and what a platform cell calls for it (IMPLICIT). The list is
  // the Worker's own manifest, which the deployer bound at deploy and the wrapper answers at getInfo before any of the
  // service's code runs. It is held per deployed hash, so a deploy with a new list is followed at once.
  // A name is exact; `*` stands for one part after com.lopecode.brain., and as the last part for one or more:
  // com.lopecode.brain.static.* or com.lopecode.brain.*.send. A path is exact.
  const IMPLICIT = ["secret.get", "db.sql", "inbox.append"].map((m) => "com.lopecode.brain." + m);
  const CALLS_MODE = "report";
  const callMatches = (pattern, name) => {
    const B = "com.lopecode.brain.";
    if (typeof pattern !== "string") return false;
    if (!pattern.includes("*")) return pattern === name;
    if (!pattern.startsWith(B) || !name.startsWith(B)) return false;
    const p = pattern.slice(B.length).split("."), n = name.slice(B.length).split("."), rest = p.at(-1) === "*";
    // A list of only * would be every method.
    if (!p.some((s) => s !== "*")) return false;
    if (rest) p.pop();
    return (rest ? n.length > p.length : n.length === p.length) && p.every((s, i) => s === "*" || s === n[i]);
  };
  const declaredBy = new Map();
  const callsOf = async (worker) => {
    const route = await settings.get("route/" + worker), held = declaredBy.get(worker);
    if (held && route && held.hash === route.hash) return held.calls;
    const short = worker.replace(/^brain-(x-)?/, "");
    if (!route || !workers.has(short)) return null;
    const r = await workers.fetch(short, new Request(`https://${short}.internal${NS}getInfo`)).catch(() => null);
    const info = r && r.ok ? await r.json().catch(() => null) : null;
    if (!info || !Array.isArray(info.calls)) return null;
    if (info.hash === route.hash) declaredBy.set(worker, { hash: route.hash, calls: info.calls });
    return info.calls;
  };
  // What was called and not declared, counted per Worker and name. At most 200 names are kept, so a Worker cannot grow the table.
  let undeclared = null;
  const note = async (worker, name) => {
    undeclared ??= new Set((await rows.list("undeclared/")).map((r) => r.key));
    const key = "undeclared/" + worker + "/" + name.slice(0, 200);
    if (!undeclared.has(key) && undeclared.size >= 200) return;
    undeclared.add(key);
    await rows.increment(key);
  };
  const callsMode = async () => (await settings.get("calls/mode")) || CALLS_MODE;
  const asDeclared = async (c, worker) => {
    const url = new URL(c.req.url);
    const name = url.pathname.startsWith("/xrpc/") ? url.pathname.slice("/xrpc/".length) : url.pathname;
    if (IMPLICIT.includes(name)) return null;
    const calls = await callsOf(worker);
    if ((calls || []).some((p) => callMatches(p, name))) return null;
    await note(worker, name);
    return (await callsMode()) === "enforce" ? fail(c, 403, "Forbidden", `${worker} did not declare a call to ${name}`) : null;
  };
  app.use("*", async (c, next) => {
    const started = Date.now();
    const who = await identify(c.req.raw);
    c.set("who", who);
    if (who.member) {
      const no = await asAuthor(c, who.member);
      if (no) return no;
    } else if (who.caller.startsWith("worker:")) {
      const no = await asDeclared(c, who.caller.slice("worker:".length));
      if (no) return no;
    }
    // Only a Worker known by its key can carry an origin. A member's Worker is checked as its author and keeps the origin too.
    const now = c.get("who");
    c.set("origin", (who.keyed && (await originFrom(c.req.header("x-brain-context"), who.keyed))) || { caller: now.caller, via: now.via || "" });
    await next();
    const done = observe(c, started).catch(() => null);
    try {
      c.executionCtx.waitUntil(done);
    } catch {}
  });
  app.onError((e, c) => fail(c, 500, "InternalServerError", String((e && e.message) || e)));
  // The kernel has already checked a token or a granted DID against the method it named.
  const allowed = (who) => who.caller === "owner" || /^(token|did):/.test(who.caller);
  const owner = async (c, next) => (allowed(c.get("who")) ? next() : fail(c, 401, "AuthRequired", "the owner"));
  const session = async (c, next) =>
    c.get("who").caller === "owner" && c.get("who").via === "session" ? next() : fail(c, 401, "AuthRequired", "the owner's own session");
  const deployerOnly = async (c, next) => (c.get("who").caller === "deployer" ? next() : fail(c, 401, "AuthRequired", "the deployer"));

  const toDeployer = async (verdict) => {
    const r = await deployer.fetch(new Request("https://deployer.internal/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.infra.verdict", { method: "POST", headers: { "content-type": "application/json" }, body: JSON.stringify(verdict) }));
    return r.ok ? r.json() : null;
  };
  // What Workers called without declaring it, and whether such a call is refused or only counted.
  app.get(NS + "calls.list", owner, async (c) =>
    c.json({
      mode: await callsMode(),
      implicit: IMPLICIT,
      undeclared: (await rows.list("undeclared/")).map(({ key, value }) => {
        const [, worker, ...name] = key.split("/");
        return { worker, method: name.join("/"), n: value };
      })
    })
  );
  app.post(NS + "calls.setMode", session, async (c) => {
    const { mode = null, clear = false } = await c.req.json().catch(() => ({}));
    if (mode !== null && !["report", "enforce"].includes(mode)) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "mode is report, enforce or null");
    if (mode === null) await settings.delete("calls/mode");
    else await settings.put("calls/mode", mode);
    if (clear) {
      for (const { key } of await rows.list("undeclared/")) await rows.delete(key);
      undeclared = null;
    }
    return c.json({ mode: await callsMode() });
  });
  // Routes and keys: written by the deployer when it deploys or removes a Worker.
  app.post(NS + "service.register", deployerOnly, async (c) => {
    const r = await c.req.json();
    const was = await rows.get("route/" + r.worker);
    // A deploy is unverified until a page has loaded its module from the Worker and run its tests.
    // The version before keeps its verdict, so a deploy that is put back returns to a version already verified.
    const same = was && r.hash && was.hash === r.hash, back = was && r.hash && was.before && was.before.hash === r.hash;
    const verified = same ? was.verified || null : back ? was.before.verified : null;
    const before = same ? was.before || null : was && was.hash && !back ? { hash: was.hash, verified: was.verified && was.verified.ok ? was.verified : null } : null;
    await settings.put("route/" + r.worker, { worker: r.worker, role: r.role, module: r.module || null, hash: r.hash || null, verified, before, methods: r.methods || {}, paths: r.paths || [], secrets: r.secrets || [], ...(r.role === "member" ? { author: r.author, off: !!(was && was.off) } : {}) });
    await rows.put("key/" + r.keyHash, { worker: r.worker, role: r.role, ...(r.role === "member" ? { author: r.author } : {}) });
    keys.delete(r.keyHash);
    declaredBy.delete(r.worker);
    return c.json({ ok: true });
  });
  app.post(NS + "service.unregister", deployerOnly, async (c) => {
    const { worker } = await c.req.json();
    await settings.delete("route/" + worker);
    for (const { key, value } of await rows.list("key/")) if (value.worker === worker) await rows.delete(key);
    keys.clear();
    return c.json({ ok: true });
  });
  // The deployer's health check of a Worker with no address of its own.
  app.post(NS + "service.health", deployerOnly, async (c) => {
    const { worker } = await c.req.json();
    const short = String(worker).replace(/^brain-(x-)?/, "");
    if (!workers.has(short)) return c.json({ ok: false, reason: "not bound yet" });
    const r = await workers.fetch(short, new Request(`https://${short}.internal/xrpc/_health`)).catch(() => null);
    return c.json(r && r.ok ? await r.json().catch(() => ({ ok: false })) : { ok: false });
  });
  // Who is a member, what each was granted and their limits: the kernel's table, sent whole each time it changes.
  app.post(NS + "people.sync", async (c) => {
    if (c.get("who").caller !== "kernel") return fail(c, 401, "AuthRequired", "the kernel");
    const { people = [] } = await c.req.json();
    const now = new Set(people.map((p) => p.did));
    for (const { key } of await rows.list("person/")) if (!now.has(key.slice("person/".length))) await rows.delete(key);
    for (const p of people) await rows.put("person/" + p.did, { did: p.did, methods: p.methods || [], quota: p.quota || null, tags: p.tags || [] });
    return c.json({ people: people.length });
  });
  // What a member needs to write a service, and how much of each limit is used.
  const idOf = async (did) => (await sha256(did)).slice(0, 10);
  app.get(NS + "member.whoami", async (c) => {
    const did = c.get("who").caller;
    const person = did.startsWith("did:") ? await rows.get("person/" + did) : null;
    if (!person) return fail(c, 403, "Forbidden", "a member");
    const id = await idOf(did);
    return c.json({ did, id, methods: MEMBER_NS + id + ".", worker: `brain-m-${id}-NAME`, files: `u/${id}/`, tables: `m_${id}_NAME_`, quota: quotaOf(person), calls: (await rows.get(`mcalls/${did}/${today()}`)) || 0 });
  });
  app.get(NS + "member.services", async (c) => {
    const who = c.get("who").caller;
    if (who !== "owner" && !who.startsWith("did:")) return fail(c, 401, "AuthRequired", "the owner or a member");
    // Another member's Worker is listed when one of its methods is for members.
    const shared = who !== "owner" && !!(await rows.get("person/" + who));
    const services = (await rows.list("route/")).map((r) => r.value).filter((r) => r.role === "member" && (who === "owner" || r.author === who || (shared && Object.values(r.methods).some((m) => m.who === "members"))));
    return c.json({ services: services.map((r) => ({ worker: r.worker, author: r.author, module: r.module, hash: r.hash, off: !!r.off, methods: Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(r.methods).map(([k, v]) => [k, v.who])) })) });
  });
  // The owner's switch. Off: nothing reaches the Worker and it reaches nothing.
  app.post(NS + "member.switch", session, async (c) => {
    const { worker, off } = await c.req.json();
    const route = await rows.get("route/" + worker);
    if (!route || route.role !== "member") return fail(c, 404, "NotFound", String(worker));
    await settings.put("route/" + worker, { ...route, off: !!off });
    return c.json({ worker, off: !!off });
  });
  // A member's Worker is not listed here: the page loads the module of every Worker this names, as whoever is
  // signed in. member.services lists them.
  app.get(NS + "service.list", async (c) => c.json({ services: (await rows.list("route/")).map((r) => r.value).filter((r) => r.role !== "member") }));
  // The page's verdict on a deploy, after it ran the module's tests. A pass marks the hash verified. A fail while
  // the hash is still unverified has the deployer put the version before back; a fail after that is only recorded.
  app.post(NS + "deploy.report", owner, async (c) => {
    const { worker, hash, ok, tests = [], reason = "" } = await c.req.json();
    const route = await rows.get("route/" + worker);
    if (!route || !route.hash || route.hash !== hash) return fail(c, 409, "Stale", `${worker} is not running ${String(hash).slice(0, 12)}`);
    const was = route.verified;
    const failed = tests.filter((t) => !t.ok).map((t) => t.name);
    const verdict = { ok: !!ok, at: Date.now(), tests: tests.length, failed, reason: String(reason).slice(0, 300) };
    if (ok) {
      await settings.put("route/" + worker, { ...route, verified: verdict });
      // Every pass is passed on: the same hash deployed again is on probation again, and only the deployer knows.
      await toDeployer({ worker, hash, ok: true });
      return c.json({ worker, hash, state: "verified" });
    }
    if (was && was.ok) {
      await settings.put("route/" + worker, { ...route, failing: verdict });
      return c.json({ worker, hash, state: "failing" });
    }
    await settings.put("route/" + worker, { ...route, verified: verdict });
    const out = await toDeployer({ worker, hash, ok: false, reason: verdict.reason || "failed: " + failed.join(", ") });
    return c.json({ worker, hash, state: out && out.state === "put-back" ? "put-back" : "failed", previous: out ? out.previous || null : null });
  });

  // Rules the owner sets without a deploy. The target is a method's NSID or a path as its service declared it.
  // Only for what a Worker declared, and not for a method its service marked fixed (secret.*). The core's own
  // methods (rule.*, service.*) are decided in this file.
  const declared = async (target) => {
    for (const { value: r } of await rows.list("route/")) {
      if (!routed(r)) continue;
      if (r.methods[target]) return { worker: r.worker, rule: r.methods[target] };
      const p = r.paths.find((x) => x.path === target);
      if (p) return { worker: r.worker, rule: p };
    }
    return null;
  };
  app.get(NS + "rule.list", owner, async (c) => {
    const set = new Map((await rows.list("rule/")).map(({ key, value }) => [key.slice("rule/".length), value]));
    const out = [];
    for (const { value: r } of await rows.list("route/")) {
      if (!routed(r)) continue;
      for (const [target, rule] of [...Object.entries(r.methods), ...r.paths.map((p) => [p.path, p])])
        out.push({ target, worker: r.worker, declared: ruleExpression(rule), set: set.has(target) ? set.get(target).allow : null, setAt: set.has(target) ? set.get(target).setAt : null });
    }
    return c.json({ rules: out.sort((a, b) => (a.target < b.target ? -1 : 1)), ttl: settings.ttl });
  });
  app.post(NS + "rule.put", session, async (c) => {
    const { target, allow } = await c.req.json();
    if (typeof allow !== "string" || !allow.trim()) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "allow is a CEL expression");
    const found = await declared(target);
    if (!found) return fail(c, 404, "NotFound", `no service declares ${target}`);
    if (found.rule.fixed) return fail(c, 403, "Forbidden", `${found.worker} fixed the rule for ${target}`);
    // A rule that does not parse is refused here, not found on the next call.
    try {
      checkedRule(target, allow);
    } catch (e) {
      return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", e.message);
    }
    await settings.put("rule/" + target, { allow, setAt: Date.now() });
    return c.json({ target, allow });
  });
  app.post(NS + "rule.delete", session, async (c) => {
    const { target } = await c.req.json();
    return c.json({ deleted: !!(await settings.delete("rule/" + target)) });
  });

  // The notebook side of the rows platform cell, one table per Worker name.
  const rowKey = (c, q) => "rows/" + (q.worker || "") + "/" + (q.key ?? q.prefix ?? "");
  app.get(NS + "rows.get", owner, async (c) => c.json({ value: await rows.get(rowKey(c, c.req.query())) }));
  app.get(NS + "rows.list", owner, async (c) => {
    const q = c.req.query(), base = "rows/" + (q.worker || "") + "/";
    return c.json({ rows: (await rows.list(base + (q.prefix || ""))).map(({ key, value }) => ({ key: key.slice(base.length), value })) });
  });
  app.post(NS + "rows.put", owner, async (c) => {
    const q = await c.req.json();
    return c.json({ ok: await rows.put(rowKey(c, q), q.value) });
  });
  app.post(NS + "rows.delete", owner, async (c) => c.json({ deleted: await rows.delete(rowKey(c, await c.req.json())) }));

  // getInfo for a named Worker, then everything a Worker declared.
  const forward = async (route, c, path) => {
    const url = new URL(c.req.url), who = c.get("who");
    const person = who.caller.startsWith("did:") ? await rows.get("person/" + who.caller) : null;
    const short = route.worker.replace(/^brain-(x-)?/, "");
    c.set("target", route.worker);
    if (!workers.has(short)) return fail(c, 502, "UpstreamUnavailable", `${route.worker} is not bound to the core`);
    const headers = new Headers(c.req.raw.headers);
    for (const name of [...headers.keys()]) if (name.startsWith("x-brain-")) headers.delete(name);
    headers.set("x-brain-caller", who.caller);
    if (who.via) headers.set("x-brain-via", who.via);
    // The origin in clear, for a Worker that decides rules of its own, and the reference it sends back on a call it makes for this one.
    const origin = c.get("origin");
    headers.set("x-brain-origin", origin.caller);
    if (origin.via) headers.set("x-brain-origin-via", origin.via);
    headers.set("x-brain-context", await contextFor(route.worker, origin));
    // What a store needs to decide for a person: that they are a member, their file limit and the tags they were granted.
    if (person) {
      headers.set("x-brain-member", "1");
      headers.set("x-brain-quota-bytes", String(quotaOf(person).bytes));
      headers.set("x-brain-tags", JSON.stringify(person.tags || []));
    }
    const bodied = !["GET", "HEAD"].includes(c.req.method);
    return workers.fetch(short, new Request("https://" + short + ".internal" + (path || url.pathname + url.search), { method: c.req.method, headers, body: bodied ? c.req.raw.body : undefined, duplex: bodied ? "half" : undefined, redirect: "manual" }));
  };
  // Prices and credits. A method or a path may have a price: one CEL expression over the caller, the origin and the
  // request, which gives US dollars. The owner's price (price.put) stands in for the one a service declared. A call
  // with no price takes none of this. A priced call is charged to the account of its origin before it is forwarded,
  // and is refused when that leaves the account over its allowance for the UTC day.
  // An account's day is one row: a list that charges and their corrections are appended to, in one statement each.
  // A charge counts when the charges that count before it, with it, are inside the allowance it was made under. That
  // is decided by the list alone, so calls made at once cannot spend past the allowance, and no call needs a lock.
  const PRICING = { owner: 1, member: 0.1, worker: 0.1, token: 0.1, perCall: 1, keepDays: 30 };
  const MICRO = 1e6, CHARGES = 2000, KEEP = 100000;
  const micro = (usd) => Math.ceil(usd * MICRO - 1e-6);
  const usd = (u) => u / MICRO;
  const pricing = async () => ({ ...PRICING, ...((await settings.get("quota/defaults")) || {}) });
  const accountOf = (origin) => {
    const o = callerOf(origin);
    return o.kind === "owner" || ["did", "token", "worker"].includes(o.kind) ? o.id : null;
  };
  const kindOf = (account) => (account === "owner" ? "owner" : account.startsWith("did:") ? "member" : account.split(":")[0]);
  const allowanceOf = async (account, p) => {
    const set = (await settings.list("quota/who/")).find((r) => r.key === "quota/who/" + account)?.value;
    return set && Number.isFinite(set.daily) ? set.daily : p[kindOf(account)] ?? 0;
  };
  const priceSet = async (target) => (await settings.list("price/")).find((r) => r.key === "price/" + target)?.value || null;
  const parsedPrice = new Map();
  const priceValue = (expression, context) => {
    try {
      if (!parsedPrice.has(expression)) parsedPrice.set(expression, cel.parse(expression));
      const v = parsedPrice.get(expression)(context), n = typeof v === "bigint" ? Number(v) : v;
      if (typeof n !== "number" || !Number.isFinite(n)) return { error: "it is not a number" };
      return n < 0 ? { error: "it is less than 0" } : { usd: n };
    } catch (e) {
      return { error: String((e && e.message) || e).split("\n")[0] };
    }
  };
  // What a day's list comes to: what is spent, and what each charge that counts still holds.
  const fold = (list) => {
    let spent = 0;
    const net = new Map();
    for (const e of list || []) {
      if (e.u != null) {
        if (spent + e.u <= e.A) (net.set(e.i, e.u), (spent += e.u));
      } else if (net.has(e.i)) {
        const back = Math.min(net.get(e.i), -e.a);
        net.set(e.i, net.get(e.i) - back);
        spent -= back;
      }
    }
    return { spent, net };
  };
  const spendKey = (day, account) => `spend/${day}/${account}`;
  // What this instance last read for an account. It stops an account that is out of credits from growing its list.
  const known = new Map();
  const charge = async (account, u, allowance, about) => {
    const day = today(), key = spendKey(day, account), A = micro(allowance), k = known.get(account);
    if (k && k.day === day && Date.now() - k.at < settings.ttl && k.spent + u > A) return { ok: false, spent: k.spent };
    const i = crypto.randomUUID().slice(0, 13);
    const n = await rows.append(key, { t: Date.now(), i, u, A, ...about }, KEEP);
    const { spent, net } = fold(await rows.get(key));
    known.set(account, { day, spent, at: Date.now() });
    if (net.has(i) && n > CHARGES) {
      await rows.append(key, { t: Date.now(), i, a: -u, r: "full" }, KEEP);
      return { ok: false, spent: spent - u, full: true };
    }
    return { ok: net.has(i), i, key, spent, account };
  };
  const giveBack = async (got, back, r) => {
    await rows.append(got.key, { t: Date.now(), i: got.i, a: -back, r }, KEEP);
    const k = known.get(got.account);
    if (k) k.spent -= back;
  };
  let pruned = "";
  const prune = async (keepDays) => {
    if (pruned === today()) return;
    pruned = today();
    for (let d = keepDays + 1; d <= keepDays + 7; d++) await rows.deletePrefix(`spend/${new Date(Date.now() - d * 86400000).toISOString().slice(0, 10)}/`);
  };
  const midnight = () => new Date(new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10) + "T00:00:00Z").getTime() + 86400000;
  const money = (n) => "$" + String(Number(n.toFixed(6)));
  const priced = async (c, route, target, rule, context) => {
    const set = await priceSet(target), expression = set ? set.price : rule.price;
    if (!expression) return forward(route, c);
    const p = await pricing(), price = priceValue(expression, context);
    if (price.error) return fail(c, 403, "Forbidden", `the price of ${target} could not be decided: ${price.error}`);
    if (price.usd > p.perCall) return fail(c, 402, "PriceOverCeiling", `${target} costs ${money(price.usd)} for this call. The most one call may cost is ${money(p.perCall)}`);
    const u = micro(price.usd);
    if (!u) return forward(route, c);
    const origin = c.get("origin"), account = accountOf(origin);
    if (!account) return fail(c, 402, "OutOfCredits", `${target} costs ${money(price.usd)} and ${callerOf(origin).id} has no credits`);
    const allowance = await allowanceOf(account, p);
    const got = await charge(account, u, allowance, { m: target, c: c.get("who").caller, o: origin.caller, v: origin.via || "" });
    if (!got.ok)
      return fail(c, 402, "OutOfCredits", got.full
        ? `${account} has made ${CHARGES} priced calls today, which is the most for one day. The count is new at 00:00 UTC`
        : `${target} costs ${money(usd(u))}. ${account} has spent ${money(usd(got.spent))} of ${money(allowance)} today. The allowance is new at 00:00 UTC, in ${Math.ceil((midnight() - Date.now()) / 60000)} minutes`);
    const old = prune(p.keepDays).catch(() => null);
    try {
      c.executionCtx.waitUntil(old);
    } catch {}
    let r;
    try {
      r = await forward(route, c);
    } catch (e) {
      await giveBack(got, u, "refund").catch(() => null);
      throw e;
    }
    let final = u;
    if (r.status < 200 || r.status >= 300) (await giveBack(got, u, "refund"), (final = 0));
    else if (r.headers.has("x-brain-cost")) {
      // The Worker may say the call cost less than its price. More, or anything that is not an amount, is not read.
      const said = r.headers.get("x-brain-cost").trim(), n = said === "" ? NaN : Number(said);
      if (Number.isFinite(n) && n >= 0 && micro(n) < u) (await giveBack(got, u - micro(n), "settle"), (final = micro(n)));
      else if (!(Number.isFinite(n) && micro(n) === u)) console.log(`brain-core: ${route.worker} said ${target} cost ${JSON.stringify(said.slice(0, 40))}; the price ${usd(u)} stands`);
    }
    const out = new Response(r.body, r);
    out.headers.set("x-brain-price", String(usd(final)));
    return out;
  };
  // One account's day as the owner reads it: each charge, what it came to, and why it changed.
  const ledgerOf = (who, list) => {
    const { net } = fold(list), why = new Map();
    for (const e of list || []) if (e.u == null && net.has(e.i)) why.set(e.i, e.r);
    return (list || []).filter((e) => e.u != null).map((e) => ({ at: e.t, who, origin: e.o + (e.v ? " (" + e.v + ")" : ""), caller: e.c, method: e.m, price: usd(e.u), cost: usd(net.get(e.i) ?? 0), counted: net.has(e.i), refunded: why.get(e.i) === "refund", change: why.get(e.i) || null }));
  };
  const isAccount = (who) => who === "owner" || /^(did|token|worker):[^\s/]+$/.test(who || "");
  const dayOf = async (account, p, day = today()) => {
    const { spent } = fold(await rows.get(spendKey(day, account))), daily = await allowanceOf(account, p);
    return { who: account, day, spent: usd(spent), daily, remaining: Math.max(0, Number((daily - usd(spent)).toFixed(6))), resetsAt: midnight() };
  };
  app.get(NS + "price.list", owner, async (c) => {
    const set = new Map((await rows.list("price/")).map(({ key, value }) => [key.slice("price/".length), value]));
    const out = [];
    for (const { value: r } of await rows.list("route/")) {
      if (!routed(r)) continue;
      for (const [target, rule] of [...Object.entries(r.methods), ...r.paths.map((p) => [p.path, p])])
        if (rule.price || set.has(target)) out.push({ target, worker: r.worker, declared: rule.price || null, set: set.has(target) ? set.get(target).price : null, setAt: set.has(target) ? set.get(target).setAt : null });
    }
    return c.json({ prices: out.sort((a, b) => (a.target < b.target ? -1 : 1)), unit: "USD", defaults: await pricing() });
  });
  app.post(NS + "price.put", session, async (c) => {
    const b = await c.req.json().catch(() => ({})), target = b.target || b.method, price = b.price;
    if (typeof price !== "string" || !price.trim()) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "price is a CEL expression that gives US dollars");
    const found = await declared(target);
    if (!found) return fail(c, 404, "NotFound", `no service declares ${target}`);
    try {
      checkedRule(target, price);
    } catch (e) {
      return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", e.message.replace("the rule", "the price"));
    }
    await settings.put("price/" + target, { price, setAt: Date.now() });
    return c.json({ target, price });
  });
  app.post(NS + "price.delete", session, async (c) => {
    const b = await c.req.json().catch(() => ({}));
    return c.json({ deleted: !!(await settings.delete("price/" + (b.target || b.method))) });
  });
  // An account reads its own day. The owner reads any.
  app.get(NS + "quota.get", async (c) => {
    const who = c.get("who"), asked = c.req.query("who"), mine = accountOf(c.get("origin"));
    if (asked && asked !== mine && who.caller !== "owner") return fail(c, 401, "AuthRequired", "the owner reads another account");
    if (!(asked || mine)) return fail(c, 401, "AuthRequired", "an account");
    if (asked && !isAccount(asked)) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "who is owner, did:…, token:NAME or worker:NAME");
    return c.json(await dayOf(asked || mine, await pricing()));
  });
  app.get(NS + "quota.list", owner, async (c) => {
    const p = await pricing(), day = today(), base = `spend/${day}/`;
    const set = new Map((await rows.list("quota/who/")).map(({ key, value }) => [key.slice("quota/who/".length), value]));
    const spent = new Map((await rows.list(base)).map(({ key, value }) => [key.slice(base.length), value]));
    const accounts = [...new Set(["owner", ...set.keys(), ...spent.keys()])].sort().map((who) => {
      const daily = set.has(who) && Number.isFinite(set.get(who).daily) ? set.get(who).daily : p[kindOf(who)] ?? 0;
      return { who, daily, set: set.has(who), spent: usd(fold(spent.get(who)).spent), charges: (spent.get(who) || []).filter((e) => e.u != null).length };
    });
    return c.json({ day, unit: "USD", resetsAt: midnight(), defaults: p, accounts });
  });
  app.post(NS + "quota.put", session, async (c) => {
    const { who, daily = null } = await c.req.json().catch(() => ({}));
    if (!isAccount(who)) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "who is owner, did:…, token:NAME or worker:NAME");
    if (daily !== null && !(typeof daily === "number" && Number.isFinite(daily) && daily >= 0)) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "daily is US dollars, 0 or more, or null for the default");
    if (daily === null) await settings.delete("quota/who/" + who);
    else await settings.put("quota/who/" + who, { daily, setAt: Date.now() });
    known.delete(who);
    return c.json(await dayOf(who, await pricing()));
  });
  app.post(NS + "quota.setDefaults", session, async (c) => {
    const b = await c.req.json().catch(() => ({})), next = { ...((await rows.get("quota/defaults")) || {}) };
    for (const k of Object.keys(PRICING)) {
      if (!(k in b)) continue;
      if (b[k] === null) delete next[k];
      else if (typeof b[k] === "number" && Number.isFinite(b[k]) && b[k] >= 0 && (k !== "keepDays" || (Number.isInteger(b[k]) && b[k] >= 1))) next[k] = b[k];
      else return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", `${k} is a number, 0 or more, or null for ${PRICING[k]}`);
    }
    await settings.put("quota/defaults", next);
    known.clear();
    return c.json({ defaults: await pricing() });
  });
  app.get(NS + "quota.ledger", owner, async (c) => {
    const day = c.req.query("day") || today(), who = c.req.query("who");
    if (!/^\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}$/.test(day)) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "day is YYYY-MM-DD");
    const base = `spend/${day}/`;
    const lists = who ? [[who, await rows.get(base + who)]] : (await rows.list(base)).map(({ key, value }) => [key.slice(base.length), value]);
    const charges = lists.flatMap(([w, list]) => ledgerOf(w, list)).sort((a, b) => b.at - a.at);
    const sum = (by) => Object.entries(charges.reduce((t, e) => ((t[e[by]] = (t[e[by]] || 0) + e.cost), t), {})).map(([k, v]) => ({ [by]: k, cost: Number(v.toFixed(6)) }));
    return c.json({ day, unit: "USD", charges: charges.slice(0, Math.min(2000, Number(c.req.query("limit")) || 200)), total: Number(charges.reduce((t, e) => t + e.cost, 0).toFixed(6)), byWho: sum("who"), byMethod: sum("method") });
  });

  // A Worker's manifest and source, for anyone. The wrapper has already answered for the core itself.
  for (const what of ["getInfo", "getSource"])
    app.get(NS + what, async (c) => {
      const name = c.req.query("worker") || "brain-core";
      const route = await settings.get("route/" + name);
      if (!route || !routed(route) || route.role === "member") return fail(c, 404, "NotFound", name);
      return forward(route, c, NS + what + "?worker=" + encodeURIComponent(name));
    });
  app.all("*", async (c) => {
    const url = new URL(c.req.url), who = c.get("who");
    // The route table and the owner's rules are read through a few seconds of memory, not from storage on every call.
    const routes = (await settings.list("route/")).map((r) => r.value).filter(routed);
    const nsid = url.pathname.startsWith("/xrpc/") ? url.pathname.slice("/xrpc/".length) : null;
    for (const route of routes) {
      const method = nsid && route.methods[nsid];
      const path = !nsid && route.paths.find((p) => p.path === url.pathname || (p.path.endsWith("/*") && url.pathname.startsWith(p.path.slice(0, -1))));
      const rule = method || path;
      if (!rule) continue;
      if (path) c.set("path", path.path);
      if (method && (method.type === "query") !== (c.req.method === "GET")) return fail(c, 405, "InvalidRequest", `${nsid} is a ${method.type}`);
      // A member's Worker answers while its author is a member and the owner has not switched it off.
      if (route.role === "member") {
        const now = await rows.get("route/" + route.worker), person = await rows.get("person/" + route.author);
        if (!now || now.off) return fail(c, 403, "Forbidden", `${route.worker} is switched off`);
        if (!person) return fail(c, 403, "Forbidden", `${route.author} is not a member`);
        if (!(await spend(person))) return fail(c, 429, "RateLimitExceeded", `${route.author} has used today's ${quotaOf(person).calls} calls`);
      }
      // The rule is one CEL expression over the caller, the origin and the request. Anything but true is a refusal.
      // A rule the owner has set for this method or path stands in for the one the service declared.
      const set = (await settings.list("rule/")).find((r) => r.key === "rule/" + (nsid || path.path))?.value;
      const context = { caller: callerOf(who), origin: callerOf(c.get("origin")), request: { method: nsid || "", path: url.pathname, verb: c.req.method, params: Object.fromEntries(url.searchParams) } };
      const verdict = decide(set ? { allow: set.allow } : rule, context);
      // Allowed, then priced: a call with a price is charged to its origin's account before it is forwarded.
      if (verdict.allow) return priced(c, route, nsid || path.path, rule, context);
      return verdict.error ? fail(c, 403, "Forbidden", "the rule for this could not be decided") : fail(c, 401, "AuthRequired", "not allowed by the rule for this");
    }
    return nsid ? fail(c, 501, "MethodNotImplemented", nsid) : c.text("not found", 404);
  });
  return app;
}
// %%

md`## Tests

The core runs under \`simulate\`. \`coreRig\` registers a kernel and one recipe the way the deployer would, then calls as each kind of caller.`
// %%
coreRig = async ({ config = {}, workers: more = {} } = {}) => {
  const seen = [], toDeployer = [];
  // What brain-x-echo's own manifest says, as the wrapper would answer at getInfo.
  const echo = { hash: "h1", calls: ["com.lopecode.brain.other.*"] };
  const sim = await simulate(core_service, {
    secrets: { BRAIN_KEY: "core-key" },
    config,
    deployer: async (request) => {
      const body = await request.json();
      toDeployer.push({ path: new URL(request.url).pathname, key: request.headers.get("x-brain-key"), body });
      return Response.json(body.ok ? { state: "kept" } : { state: "put-back", previous: "h0" });
    },
    workers: {
      echo: async (request) => {
        if (request.url === "https://echo.internal/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.getInfo") return Response.json({ name: "brain-x-echo", hash: echo.hash, calls: echo.calls });
        const body = ["GET", "HEAD"].includes(request.method) ? null : new TextDecoder().decode(await request.arrayBuffer());
        seen.push({ url: request.url, method: request.method, caller: request.headers.get("x-brain-caller"), cookie: request.headers.get("cookie"), key: request.headers.get("x-brain-key"), body });
        return request.url.includes("/redirect") ? new Response(null, { status: 302, headers: { location: "https://example.com/" } }) : Response.json({ echoed: new URL(request.url).pathname });
      },
      ...more
    }
  });
  const X = "/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.";
  const send = (base, headers) => async (path, body, extra = {}) => {
    const r = await sim.fetch(base + (path.startsWith("/") ? path : X + path), {
      method: body === undefined ? "GET" : "POST",
      headers: { ...headers, ...extra, ...(body === undefined ? {} : { "content-type": "application/json" }) },
      body: body === undefined ? undefined : typeof body === "string" || body instanceof Uint8Array ? body : JSON.stringify(body),
      redirect: "manual"
    });
    const text = await r.text();
    let data = text;
    try { data = JSON.parse(text); } catch {}
    return { status: r.status, data, headers: r.headers };
  };
  // Another Worker's answer to anything: it keeps who the core said was calling and for whom.
  const heard = [];
  const hear = (worker) => async (request) => (heard.push({ worker, caller: request.headers.get("x-brain-caller"), origin: request.headers.get("x-brain-origin"), via: request.headers.get("x-brain-origin-via"), context: request.headers.get("x-brain-context") }), Response.json({ ok: true }));
  const deployer = send("https://cb-core.sub.workers.dev", { "x-brain-deployer": "core-key" });
  const as = (caller, via = "session") => send("https://core.internal", { "x-brain-key": "kernel-key", "x-brain-caller": caller, "x-brain-via": via });
  const worker = send("https://core.internal", { "x-brain-key": "echo-key", "x-brain-caller": "owner" });
  await deployer("service.register", { worker: "brain", role: "kernel", methods: {}, paths: [], secrets: [], keyHash: await sha256("kernel-key") });
  await deployer("service.register", {
    worker: "brain-x-echo",
    role: "recipe",
    methods: { "com.lopecode.brain.echo.say": { type: "procedure", who: "owner" }, "com.lopecode.brain.echo.read": { type: "query", who: "anyone" }, "com.lopecode.brain.echo.key": { type: "query", who: "owner", fixed: true } },
    paths: [{ path: "/hooks/echo", who: "anyone" }, { path: "/redirect", who: "anyone" }, { path: "/private", who: "owner" }],
    secrets: ["ECHO_KEY"],
    hash: "h1",
    module: "@tomlarkworthy/echo",
    keyHash: await sha256("echo-key")
  });
  return { sim, seen, toDeployer, deployer, as, worker, echo, heard, hear, send, owner: as("owner"), anonymous: as("anonymous", ""), nobody: send("https://core.internal", {}) };
}
// %%
test_calls_are_counted_and_handed_to_the_metrics_service = {
  const batches = [];
  const workers = {
    metrics: async (request) => (batches.push({ caller: request.headers.get("x-brain-caller"), ...(await request.json()) }), Response.json({ stored: 1 })),
    broken: async () => new Response("boom", { status: 500 })
  };
  const settle = () => new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 20));
  // The counter is the Worker's own state and outlives a rig, so both waits are set to nothing here.
  const rig = await coreRig({ config: { metricsFlushMs: 0, metricsRouteMs: 0 }, workers });
  const reg = (worker, methods) => rig.deployer("service.register", { worker, role: "recipe", methods, paths: [], secrets: [], keyHash: worker });
  await reg("brain-x-metrics", { "com.lopecode.brain.metrics.record": { type: "procedure", who: "worker:brain-core" }, "com.lopecode.brain.metrics.query": { type: "query", who: "owner" } });
  await reg("brain-x-broken", { "com.lopecode.brain.broken.go": { type: "procedure", who: "owner" } });
  await settle();
  batches.length = 0;
  await rig.owner("echo.say", { text: "hi" });
  await rig.anonymous("/hooks/echo");
  await rig.anonymous("made.up.name");
  await rig.owner("broken.go", {});
  // Its own traffic is not counted.
  await rig.owner("metrics.query");
  await settle();
  expect(batches.every((b) => b.caller === "worker:brain-core")).toBe(true);
  const got = batches.flatMap((b) => b.buckets).map((b) => [b.worker, b.method, b.caller, b.status, b.n]);
  // The broken Worker here is a bare function with no wrapper, so it names no version; the core names its own.
  expect(batches.flatMap((b) => b.buckets).map((b) => b.version)).toEqual(["", "", rig.sim.emitted.hash.slice(0, 12), ""]);
  expect(got).toEqual([
    ["brain-x-echo", "echo.say", "owner", 200, 1],
    ["brain-x-echo", "/hooks/echo", "anonymous", 200, 1],
    ["brain-core", "(unknown)", "anonymous", 501, 1],
    ["brain-x-broken", "broken.go", "owner", 500, 1]
  ]);
  expect(batches.flatMap((b) => b.errors)).toMatchObject([{ worker: "brain-x-broken", method: "broken.go", status: 500 }]);
  return got.length + " counted";
}
// %%
test_routes_by_method_and_path = {
  const rig = await coreRig();
  expect((await rig.owner("echo.say", { text: "hi" })).data).toEqual({ echoed: "/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.echo.say" });
  expect(rig.seen[0]).toMatchObject({ method: "POST", caller: "owner", body: '{"text":"hi"}', key: null });
  expect((await rig.anonymous("/hooks/echo?hub.challenge=7")).status).toBe(200);
  expect(rig.seen[1]).toMatchObject({ caller: "anonymous", url: "https://echo.internal/hooks/echo?hub.challenge=7" });
  // A redirect from a recipe reaches the caller as a redirect.
  expect((await rig.anonymous("/redirect")).status).toBe(302);
  expect((await rig.owner("nothing.here")).data).toEqual({ error: "MethodNotImplemented", message: "com.lopecode.brain.nothing.here" });
  expect((await rig.owner("/nowhere")).status).toBe(404);
  return rig.seen.length + " forwarded";
}
// %%
test_a_deploy_is_unverified_until_its_tests_are_reported = {
  const rig = await coreRig();
  const echo = async () => (await rig.owner("service.list")).data.services.find((s) => s.worker === "brain-x-echo");
  expect(await echo()).toMatchObject({ hash: "h1", module: "@tomlarkworthy/echo", verified: null });
  // Not the owner, or not the hash that is running: nothing changes.
  expect((await rig.anonymous("deploy.report", { worker: "brain-x-echo", hash: "h1", ok: true })).status).toBe(401);
  expect((await rig.owner("deploy.report", { worker: "brain-x-echo", hash: "old", ok: false })).data.error).toBe("Stale");
  expect(rig.toDeployer).toEqual([]);
  // A fail while unverified goes to the deployer, which puts the version before back.
  const failed = await rig.owner("deploy.report", { worker: "brain-x-echo", hash: "h1", ok: false, tests: [{ name: "test_a", ok: true }, { name: "test_b", ok: false }] });
  expect(failed.data).toEqual({ worker: "brain-x-echo", hash: "h1", state: "put-back", previous: "h0" });
  expect(rig.toDeployer[0]).toMatchObject({ path: "/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.infra.verdict", key: "core-key", body: { worker: "brain-x-echo", hash: "h1", ok: false, reason: "failed: test_b" } });
  expect((await echo()).verified).toMatchObject({ ok: false, failed: ["test_b"] });
  // A pass marks it verified and tells the deployer, each time.
  expect((await rig.owner("deploy.report", { worker: "brain-x-echo", hash: "h1", ok: true, tests: [{ name: "test_a", ok: true }] })).data.state).toBe("verified");
  expect((await rig.owner("deploy.report", { worker: "brain-x-echo", hash: "h1", ok: true })).data.state).toBe("verified");
  expect(rig.toDeployer.map((g) => g.body.ok)).toEqual([false, true, true]);
  // A fail after that is recorded and nothing is put back.
  expect((await rig.owner("deploy.report", { worker: "brain-x-echo", hash: "h1", ok: false, tests: [{ name: "test_a", ok: false }] })).data.state).toBe("failing");
  expect(rig.toDeployer.length).toBe(3);
  expect(await echo()).toMatchObject({ verified: { ok: true }, failing: { failed: ["test_a"] } });
  // The same hash registered again stays verified; a new hash starts unverified.
  const again = { worker: "brain-x-echo", role: "recipe", methods: {}, paths: [], secrets: [], keyHash: await sha256("echo-key") };
  await rig.deployer("service.register", { ...again, hash: "h1" });
  expect((await echo()).verified.ok).toBe(true);
  await rig.deployer("service.register", { ...again, hash: "h2" });
  expect((await echo()).verified).toBe(null);
  // Put back to h1: the verdict it had comes back with it.
  await rig.deployer("service.register", { ...again, hash: "h1" });
  expect((await echo()).verified.ok).toBe(true);
  return "unverified, put back, verified, failing";
}
// %%
test_a_worker_calls_a_method_not_a_worker = {
  const rig = await coreRig();
  await rig.deployer("service.register", {
    worker: "brain-x-other", role: "recipe", keyHash: await sha256("other-key"), paths: [], secrets: [],
    methods: { "com.lopecode.brain.other.forWorkers": { type: "procedure", who: "workers" }, "com.lopecode.brain.other.forEcho": { type: "procedure", who: "worker:brain-x-echo" }, "com.lopecode.brain.other.forOwner": { type: "procedure", who: "owner" } }
  });
  // No binding to brain-x-other in this rig: 502 means the core let the call through and tried to forward it.
  const status = async (method) => (await rig.worker(method, {})).status;
  expect([await status("other.forWorkers"), await status("other.forEcho"), await status("other.forOwner")]).toEqual([502, 502, 401]);
  expect((await rig.anonymous("other.forWorkers", {})).status).toBe(401);
  // The deployer is let through where any Worker is, and nowhere else.
  const asDeployer = async (method) => (await rig.deployer(method, {})).status;
  expect([await asDeployer("other.forWorkers"), await asDeployer("other.forEcho"), await asDeployer("other.forOwner")]).toEqual([502, 401, 401]);
  // Anyone may read a Worker's manifest and source: the core passes the question on.
  expect((await rig.anonymous("getSource?worker=brain-x-echo")).status).toBe(200);
  expect(rig.seen.at(-1)).toMatchObject({ url: "https://echo.internal/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.getSource?worker=brain-x-echo" });
  expect((await rig.anonymous("getSource?worker=brain-x-nobody")).status).toBe(404);
  return "by method";
}
// %%
test_a_worker_calls_only_what_its_service_declared = {
  const rig = await coreRig();
  const O = "com.lopecode.brain.other.";
  await rig.deployer("service.register", { worker: "brain-x-other", role: "recipe", keyHash: await sha256("other-key"), paths: [{ path: "/hooks/other", who: "anyone" }], secrets: [], methods: { [O + "a"]: { type: "procedure", who: "workers" }, [O + "b.send"]: { type: "procedure", who: "workers" }, [O + "c"]: { type: "procedure", who: "workers" } } });
  const mode = (m) => rig.owner("calls.setMode", { mode: m });
  const status = async (method, body = {}) => (await rig.worker(method, body)).status;
  await mode("enforce");
  // 502: the core let the call through and has no binding to brain-x-other in this rig.
  rig.echo.calls = [O + "a"];
  expect([await status("other.a"), await status("other.c")]).toEqual([502, 403]);
  expect((await rig.worker("other.c", {})).data).toEqual({ error: "Forbidden", message: "brain-x-echo did not declare a call to com.lopecode.brain.other.c" });
  // The list is held for the deployed hash: the same hash is not asked again, a new deploy is.
  rig.echo.calls = [O + "a", O + "c"];
  expect(await status("other.c")).toBe(403);
  rig.echo.hash = "h2";
  await rig.deployer("service.register", { worker: "brain-x-echo", role: "recipe", hash: "h2", methods: {}, paths: [], secrets: [], keyHash: await sha256("echo-key") });
  expect(await status("other.c")).toBe(502);
  // * is one part; as the last part it is one or more.
  rig.echo.calls = ["com.lopecode.brain.*.b.send", "*", "com.lopecode.*", "com.lopecode.brain.*", "com.lopecode.brain.*.*"];
  rig.echo.hash = "h3";
  await rig.deployer("service.register", { worker: "brain-x-echo", role: "recipe", hash: "h3", methods: {}, paths: [], secrets: [], keyHash: await sha256("echo-key") });
  expect([await status("other.b.send"), await status("other.a"), await status("other.c")]).toEqual([502, 403, 403]);
  // What a platform cell calls is not declared. These reach the routing: no Worker in this rig declares them.
  expect([await status("inbox.append"), await status("db.sql"), (await rig.worker("secret.get?name=A")).status]).toEqual([501, 501, 501]);
  // The core's own methods and a path are calls too.
  expect([(await rig.worker("service.list")).status, (await rig.worker("/hooks/other")).status]).toEqual([403, 403]);
  // The kernel and the deployer are not Workers of a service: nothing is declared for them.
  expect([(await rig.owner("other.a", {})).status, (await rig.deployer("other.a", {})).status]).toEqual([502, 502]);
  // A Worker whose manifest cannot be read has declared nothing.
  await rig.deployer("service.register", { worker: "brain-x-other", role: "recipe", keyHash: await sha256("other-key"), paths: [], secrets: [], methods: { [O + "a"]: { type: "procedure", who: "workers" } } });
  const other = await rig.sim.fetch("https://core.internal/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.echo.read", { headers: { "x-brain-key": "other-key" } });
  expect([other.status, (await other.json()).message]).toEqual([403, "brain-x-other did not declare a call to com.lopecode.brain.echo.read"]);
  // Counted, by Worker and name. Only the owner's own session changes the mode.
  const listed = (await rig.owner("calls.list")).data;
  expect([listed.mode, listed.implicit.length]).toEqual(["enforce", 3]);
  expect(Object.fromEntries(listed.undeclared.map((u) => [u.worker + " " + u.method.replace("com.lopecode.brain.", ""), u.n]))).toEqual({ "brain-x-echo other.c": 4, "brain-x-echo other.a": 1, "brain-x-echo service.list": 1, "brain-x-echo /hooks/other": 1, "brain-x-other echo.read": 1 });
  expect([(await rig.as("owner", "jwt")("calls.setMode", { mode: "report" })).status, (await rig.worker("calls.setMode", { mode: "report" })).status, (await rig.owner("calls.setMode", { mode: "off" })).status]).toEqual([401, 403, 400]);
  // report: counted and let through.
  expect((await mode("report")).data).toEqual({ mode: "report" });
  expect(await status("other.a")).toBe(502);
  expect((await rig.owner("calls.list")).data.undeclared.find((u) => u.method === O + "a").n).toBe(2);
  // clear empties the counts; null puts the mode back to the default.
  expect((await rig.owner("calls.setMode", { mode: null, clear: true })).data).toEqual({ mode: "report" });
  expect((await rig.owner("calls.list")).data.undeclared).toEqual([]);
  return listed.undeclared.length + " names counted";
}
// %%
test_a_rule_can_be_an_expression = {
  const rig = await coreRig();
  const X = "com.lopecode.brain.other.";
  await rig.deployer("service.register", {
    worker: "brain-x-other", role: "recipe", keyHash: await sha256("other-key"), secrets: [],
    methods: {
      [X + "friends"]: { type: "procedure", who: "owner", allow: 'caller.did in ["did:plc:friend"]' },
      [X + "read"]: { type: "query", who: "owner", allow: 'caller.trusted || request.params.name.startsWith("pub/")' },
      [X + "broken"]: { type: "procedure", who: "anyone", allow: "caller.nothing == 1" }
    },
    paths: [{ path: "/open/*", allow: 'request.verb == "GET"' }]
  });
  // No binding to brain-x-other in this rig: 502 means the core let the call through and tried to forward it.
  expect((await rig.as("did:plc:friend", "jwt")("other.friends", {})).status).toBe(502);
  expect((await rig.as("did:plc:stranger", "jwt")("other.friends", {})).status).toBe(401);
  // The expression is the whole decision: this one does not name the owner.
  expect((await rig.owner("other.friends", {})).status).toBe(401);
  expect((await rig.anonymous("other.read?name=pub/a")).status).toBe(502);
  expect((await rig.anonymous("other.read?name=private/a")).status).toBe(401);
  expect((await rig.owner("other.read?name=private/a")).status).toBe(502);
  // A rule that cannot be decided refuses, and says so without the expression.
  const none = await rig.anonymous("other.read");
  expect([none.status, none.data.error]).toEqual([403, "Forbidden"]);
  expect((await rig.owner("other.broken", {})).status).toBe(403);
  expect((await rig.anonymous("/open/a")).status).toBe(502);
  expect((await rig.anonymous("/open/a", {})).status).toBe(401);
  return "by DID, by parameter, by verb";
}
// %%
test_the_owner_sets_a_rule_without_a_deploy = {
  const rig = await coreRig();
  // echo.say is declared for the owner. 200 is the echo recipe answering.
  expect((await rig.anonymous("echo.say", {})).status).toBe(401);
  const put = await rig.owner("rule.put", { target: "com.lopecode.brain.echo.say", allow: 'caller.kind == "anonymous" || caller.session' });
  expect([put.status, put.data.target]).toEqual([200, "com.lopecode.brain.echo.say"]);
  expect((await rig.anonymous("echo.say", {})).status).toBe(200);
  // The set rule stands in for the declared one: a token passed the declared rule and does not pass this.
  expect((await rig.as("token:laptop", "token")("echo.say", {})).status).toBe(401);
  const listed = (await rig.owner("rule.list")).data.rules.find((r) => r.target === "com.lopecode.brain.echo.say");
  expect(listed).toMatchObject({ worker: "brain-x-echo", declared: "caller.trusted", set: 'caller.kind == "anonymous" || caller.session' });
  // Only the owner's own session sets one; it must parse; it must name something a Worker declared.
  expect((await rig.as("token:laptop", "token")("rule.put", { target: "com.lopecode.brain.echo.say", allow: "true" })).status).toBe(401);
  expect((await rig.worker("rule.put", { target: "com.lopecode.brain.echo.say", allow: "true" })).status).toBe(401);
  expect((await rig.owner("rule.put", { target: "com.lopecode.brain.echo.say", allow: "caller.kind ==" })).status).toBe(400);
  expect((await rig.owner("rule.put", { target: "com.lopecode.brain.rule.put", allow: "true" })).status).toBe(404);
  // A method its service marked fixed keeps the declared rule.
  expect((await rig.owner("rule.put", { target: "com.lopecode.brain.echo.key", allow: "true" })).status).toBe(403);
  expect((await rig.anonymous("echo.key")).status).toBe(401);
  expect((await rig.owner("rule.delete", { target: "com.lopecode.brain.echo.say" })).data).toEqual({ deleted: true });
  expect((await rig.anonymous("echo.say", {})).status).toBe(401);
  expect((await rig.as("token:laptop", "token")("echo.say", {})).status).toBe(200);
  return "set, listed, refused 4 ways, deleted";
}
// %%
test_owner_methods_refuse_other_callers = {
  const rig = await coreRig();
  expect((await rig.anonymous("echo.say", {})).status).toBe(401);
  expect((await rig.anonymous("/private")).status).toBe(401);
  expect((await rig.anonymous("echo.read")).status).toBe(200);
  expect((await rig.anonymous("rule.list")).status).toBe(401);
  // A token or a granted DID has been checked against the method by the kernel.
  expect((await rig.as("token:laptop", "token")("echo.say", {})).status).toBe(200);
  // No key, or a recipe claiming to be the owner, is not the owner.
  expect((await rig.nobody("rule.list", undefined, { "x-brain-caller": "owner" })).status).toBe(401);
  expect((await rig.worker("rule.list")).status).toBe(401);
  expect((await rig.worker("service.register", { worker: "brain-x-echo", role: "kernel", keyHash: "x" })).status).toBe(401);
  expect(rig.seen.length).toBe(2);
  return "401 for anonymous, keyless and a recipe naming itself owner";
}
// %%
test_notebook_rows_per_worker = {
  const rig = await coreRig();
  await rig.owner("rows.put", { worker: "whatsapp", key: "linked", value: "+4915" });
  await rig.owner("rows.put", { worker: "digest", key: "linked", value: "other" });
  expect((await rig.owner("rows.get?worker=whatsapp&key=linked")).data).toEqual({ value: "+4915" });
  expect((await rig.owner("rows.list?worker=whatsapp")).data.rows).toEqual([{ key: "linked", value: "+4915" }]);
  expect((await rig.anonymous("rows.get?worker=whatsapp&key=linked")).status).toBe(401);
  return "two tables";
}
// %%
md`## Members

A member's Worker (\`brain-m-ID-NAME\`, deployed by the deployer for a member) has its author's permissions and no others.

| | |
|---|---|
| \`people.sync\` | procedure, the kernel. \`{ people: [{ did, methods, quota, tags }] }\`: every member, what each was granted, their limits and their tag grants. Sent whole on each change; a DID left out is no longer a member. |
| A call a member's Worker makes | Allowed when its author is a member, the Worker is not switched off, and the method is \`db.sql\`, a \`static.*\` method, a member's method (\`com.lopecode.brain.m.…\`) or in the author's grant. It goes on as a call by the author's DID with \`x-brain-via: worker:brain-m-ID-NAME\`. A path that is not a method is refused. |
| A call to a member's Worker | Decided by the rule the deployer wrote for the method, and refused while the Worker is off or its author is not a member. |
| \`member.whoami\` | query, a member. Their ID, the names their methods, Workers, files and tables take, their limits and today's calls. |
| \`member.services\` | query. The owner sees every member's Workers; a member their own and any with a method for members. |
| \`member.switch\` | procedure, the owner's session. \`{ worker, off }\` |
| \`service.health\` | procedure, the deployer. Asks a Worker that has no address for its health, over its binding. |
| Limits | 2000 calls a UTC day into and out of one member's Workers, 20 MB of files, 3 Workers; each is the owner's to change per member (\`people.put\`, \`quota\`). |
| Storage | \`person/<did>\`, \`mcalls/<did>/<day>\` |

Membership, a grant and the switch are read from storage on each call, so a change holds from the next one.`
// %%
memberCoreRig = async () => {
  const A = "did:plc:alice", B = "did:plc:bob", W = "brain-m-aaaaaaaaaa-todo", ns = "com.lopecode.brain.m.aaaaaaaaaa.";
  const heard = [];
  const rig = await coreRig({
    workers: {
      "m-aaaaaaaaaa-todo": async (request) => {
        heard.push({ path: new URL(request.url).pathname, caller: request.headers.get("x-brain-caller"), via: request.headers.get("x-brain-via"), context: request.headers.get("x-brain-context") });
        return new URL(request.url).pathname === "/xrpc/_health" ? Response.json({ ok: true, hash: "m1" }) : Response.json({ served: true });
      }
    }
  });
  await rig.deployer("service.register", {
    worker: W, role: "member", author: A, hash: "m1", module: "@alice/todo", paths: [], secrets: [], keyHash: await sha256("todo-key"),
    methods: { [ns + "add"]: { type: "procedure", who: "author", allow: 'caller.kind == "owner" || caller.did == "did:plc:alice"' }, [ns + "list"]: { type: "query", who: "members", allow: 'caller.kind in ["owner", "did"]' } }
  });
  const kernel = rig.as("kernel", "");
  const sync = (people) => kernel("people.sync", { people });
  // The Worker itself, claiming to be the owner.
  const todo = async (path, body) => {
    const r = await rig.sim.fetch("https://core.internal" + (path.startsWith("/") ? path : "/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain." + path), { method: body === undefined ? "GET" : "POST", headers: { "x-brain-key": "todo-key", "x-brain-caller": "owner", "x-brain-via": "session", ...(body === undefined ? {} : { "content-type": "application/json" }) }, body: body === undefined ? undefined : JSON.stringify(body) });
    return { status: r.status, data: await r.json().catch(() => null) };
  };
  return { ...rig, A, B, W, ns, heard, others: rig.heard, sync, todo, kernel };
}
// %%
// Three Workers in a row: a, b and c. b.go is for a acting for a trusted origin; c.go is for b acting for the owner's own tab.
originRig = async (config = {}) => {
  const rig = await coreRig({ config, workers: {} });
  const P = "com.lopecode.brain.";
  const workers = { a: rig.hear("a"), b: rig.hear("b"), c: rig.hear("c") };
  for (const [name, handler] of Object.entries(workers)) rig.sim.env["X_" + name.toUpperCase()] = { fetch: async (request) => (request.url.endsWith("getInfo") ? Response.json({ name: "brain-x-" + name, hash: "h", calls: [P + "*.go", P + "*.who"] }) : handler(request)) };
  const reg = async (name, methods) => rig.deployer("service.register", { worker: "brain-x-" + name, role: "recipe", methods, paths: [], secrets: [], hash: "h", keyHash: await sha256(name + "-key") });
  await reg("a", { [P + "a.go"]: { type: "procedure", who: "anyone" } });
  await reg("b", { [P + "b.go"]: { type: "procedure", allow: 'caller.worker == "brain-x-a" && origin.trusted' }, [P + "b.who"]: { type: "procedure", who: "workers" } });
  await reg("c", { [P + "c.go"]: { type: "procedure", allow: 'caller.worker == "brain-x-b" && origin.session' } });
  // A call by Worker `name`, with the reference it was given or any other text.
  const from = (name, context) => rig.send("https://core.internal", { "x-brain-key": name + "-key", "x-brain-caller": "owner", "x-brain-via": "session", "x-brain-origin": "owner", ...(context ? { "x-brain-context": context } : {}) });
  // What the last call to a Worker carried.
  const last = (worker) => rig.heard.filter((h) => h.worker === worker).at(-1);
  // `who` calls a.go; a then calls `method` with the reference it was given.
  const chain = async (who, method, body = {}) => {
    await who("a.go", {});
    return from("a", last("a").context)(method, body);
  };
  return { ...rig, from, last, chain };
}
// %%
test_the_origin_of_a_call_is_who_started_the_chain = {
  const rig = await originRig();
  // From outside the origin is the caller.
  await rig.owner("a.go", {});
  expect(rig.last("a")).toMatchObject({ caller: "owner", origin: "owner", via: "session" });
  await rig.anonymous("a.go", {});
  expect(rig.last("a")).toMatchObject({ caller: "anonymous", origin: "anonymous", via: null });
  // A Worker that sends the reference back calls for the origin; one that does not calls for itself.
  expect((await rig.chain(rig.owner, "b.go")).status).toBe(200);
  expect(rig.last("b")).toMatchObject({ caller: "worker:brain-x-a", origin: "owner", via: "session" });
  expect((await rig.chain(rig.as("did:plc:ada", "jwt"), "b.go")).status).toBe(200);
  expect(rig.last("b")).toMatchObject({ caller: "worker:brain-x-a", origin: "did:plc:ada", via: "jwt" });
  expect((await rig.chain(rig.as("owner", "turn:7"), "b.go")).status).toBe(200);
  expect(rig.last("b")).toMatchObject({ origin: "owner", via: "turn:7" });
  // The same rule, the same Worker, and an origin nobody checked: refused.
  expect((await rig.chain(rig.anonymous, "b.go")).status).toBe(401);
  expect((await rig.from("a")("b.go", {})).status).toBe(401);
  // What a Worker says in clear is not read.
  expect((await rig.from("a")("b.who", {})).status).toBe(200);
  expect(rig.last("b")).toMatchObject({ caller: "worker:brain-x-a", origin: "worker:brain-x-a", via: null });
  // Three in a row keep the first origin, and each reference is for one Worker.
  await rig.chain(rig.owner, "b.go");
  expect((await rig.from("b", rig.last("b").context)("c.go", {})).status).toBe(200);
  expect(rig.last("c")).toMatchObject({ caller: "worker:brain-x-b", origin: "owner", via: "session" });
  await rig.chain(rig.as("owner", "turn:7"), "b.go");
  expect((await rig.from("b", rig.last("b").context)("c.go", {})).status).toBe(401);
  return rig.heard.length + " forwarded";
}
// %%
test_a_reference_that_is_not_the_cores_own_gives_no_origin = {
  const rig = await originRig();
  await rig.owner("a.go", {});
  const good = rig.last("a").context, [v, payload, sig] = good.split(".");
  expect(JSON.parse(atob(payload.replace(/-/g, "+").replace(/_/g, "/")))).toMatchObject({ o: "owner", v: "session", w: "brain-x-a" });
  expect((await rig.from("a", good)("b.go", {})).status).toBe(200);
  // Changed, signed by somebody else, cut short, or not one at all.
  const forged = btoa(JSON.stringify({ o: "owner", v: "session", w: "brain-x-a", e: Date.now() + 60000 })).replace(/=+$/, "");
  for (const bad of [[v, forged, sig].join("."), [v, payload, sig.slice(0, -1) + (sig.endsWith("A") ? "B" : "A")].join("."), [v, payload].join("."), "owner", "c1.e30.x"]) {
    expect([bad.slice(0, 12), (await rig.from("a", bad)("b.go", {})).status]).toEqual([bad.slice(0, 12), 401]);
    expect((await rig.from("a", bad)("b.who", {})).status).toBe(200);
    expect(rig.last("b").origin).toBe("worker:brain-x-a");
  }
  // Made for another Worker: b was given its own, and a cannot use it, nor b a's.
  const forB = rig.last("b").context;
  await rig.from("a", good)("b.go", {});
  expect((await rig.from("a", rig.last("b").context)("b.go", {})).status).toBe(401);
  expect((await rig.from("b", good)("c.go", {})).status).toBe(401);
  expect(forB).not.toBe(good);
  // The kernel is not a Worker of a service: a reference it passes on is not read.
  await rig.send("https://core.internal", { "x-brain-key": "kernel-key", "x-brain-caller": "anonymous", "x-brain-context": good })("a.go", {});
  expect(rig.last("a").origin).toBe("anonymous");
  // Ended.
  const short = await originRig({ contextMs: -1 });
  await short.owner("a.go", {});
  expect((await short.from("a", short.last("a").context)("b.go", {})).status).toBe(401);
  return "5 refused, 2 for another Worker, 1 ended";
}
// %%
test_a_members_worker_keeps_its_author_and_carries_an_origin = {
  const rig = await memberCoreRig(), { A, W } = rig;
  rig.sim.env.X_B = { fetch: rig.hear("b") };
  const P = "com.lopecode.brain.";
  await rig.deployer("service.register", { worker: "brain-x-b", role: "recipe", methods: { [P + "b.go"]: { type: "procedure", allow: "caller.did == " + JSON.stringify(A) + " && origin.session" }, [P + "b.who"]: { type: "procedure", who: "owner" } }, paths: [], secrets: [], hash: "h", keyHash: await sha256("b-key") });
  await rig.sync([{ did: A, methods: [P + "b.go", P + "b.who"] }]);
  const todo = (context) => rig.send("https://core.internal", { "x-brain-key": "todo-key", ...(context ? { "x-brain-context": context } : {}) });
  // With no reference the origin is its author, named with the Worker.
  expect((await todo()("b.who", {})).status).toBe(200);
  expect(rig.others.at(-1)).toMatchObject({ caller: A, origin: A, via: "worker:" + W });
  expect((await todo()("b.go", {})).status).toBe(401);
  // The owner calls the member's method; the Worker calls on with the reference: still checked as its author, and for the owner.
  expect((await rig.owner(rig.ns.slice(P.length) + "list")).status).toBe(200);
  const given = rig.heard.at(-1).context;
  expect((await todo(given)("b.go", {})).status).toBe(200);
  expect(rig.others.at(-1)).toMatchObject({ caller: A, origin: "owner", via: "session" });
  // The author's grant is still what is checked.
  await rig.sync([{ did: A, methods: [] }]);
  expect((await todo(given)("b.go", {})).status).toBe(403);
  return "as its author, for the owner";
}
// %%

test_a_members_worker_calls_as_its_author_and_no_more = {
  const rig = await memberCoreRig(), { A, B, W } = rig;
  // Before the kernel has named any member, it may call nothing.
  expect((await rig.todo("echo.read")).status).toBe(403);
  await rig.sync([{ did: A, methods: ["com.lopecode.brain.echo.say"] }, { did: B, methods: [] }]);
  expect((await rig.todo("echo.say", {})).status).toBe(200);
  expect(rig.seen.at(-1).caller).toBe(A);
  // Not granted to its author: refused, whoever may otherwise call it.
  expect((await rig.todo("echo.read")).data.message).toBe(`${W} runs as ${A}, who has no grant for com.lopecode.brain.echo.read`);
  expect((await rig.todo("echo.key")).status).toBe(403);
  expect((await rig.todo("rows.get?worker=brain-x-echo&key=a")).status).toBe(403);
  expect((await rig.todo("member.switch", { worker: W, off: false })).status).toBe(403);
  expect((await rig.todo("people.sync", { people: [] })).status).toBe(403);
  expect((await rig.todo("/hooks/echo")).status).toBe(403);
  // The grant is read on each call.
  await rig.sync([{ did: A, methods: [] }, { did: B, methods: [] }]);
  expect((await rig.todo("echo.say", {})).status).toBe(403);
  await rig.sync([{ did: A, methods: ["com.lopecode.brain.echo.say"] }, { did: B, methods: [] }]);
  expect((await rig.todo("echo.say", {})).status).toBe(200);
  // Removed: nothing in, nothing out.
  await rig.sync([{ did: B, methods: [] }]);
  expect((await rig.todo("echo.say", {})).data.message).toBe(`${A} is not a member, so ${W} may call nothing`);
  expect((await rig.as(B)("m.aaaaaaaaaa.list")).status).toBe(403);
  expect((await rig.owner("people.sync", { people: [] })).status).toBe(401);
  expect((await rig.as(B)("people.sync", { people: [] })).status).toBe(401);
}
// %%
test_a_members_method_is_open_by_its_rule_and_the_owner_has_a_switch = {
  const rig = await memberCoreRig(), { A, B, W, ns } = rig;
  await rig.sync([{ did: A, methods: [] }, { did: B, methods: [] }]);
  const add = "m.aaaaaaaaaa.add", list = "m.aaaaaaaaaa.list";
  expect([(await rig.as(A)(add, {})).status, (await rig.as(B)(add, {})).status, (await rig.owner(add, {})).status, (await rig.anonymous(add, {})).status]).toEqual([200, 401, 200, 401]);
  expect([(await rig.as(A)(list)).status, (await rig.as(B)(list)).status, (await rig.anonymous(list)).status]).toEqual([200, 200, 401]);
  expect(rig.heard.at(-1)).toMatchObject({ caller: B });
  // Its own method through the core arrives as its author, with the Worker named.
  expect((await rig.todo(list)).status).toBe(200);
  expect(rig.heard.at(-1)).toMatchObject({ path: "/xrpc/" + ns + "list", caller: A, via: "worker:" + W });
  expect((await rig.as(A)("member.services")).data.services).toEqual([{ worker: W, author: A, module: "@alice/todo", hash: "m1", off: false, methods: { [ns + "add"]: "author", [ns + "list"]: "members" } }]);
  // Another member sees it because list is for members; someone who is not a member sees nothing.
  expect((await rig.as(B)("member.services")).data.services.map((s) => s.worker)).toEqual([W]);
  expect((await rig.as("did:plc:stranger")("member.services")).data.services).toEqual([]);
  expect((await rig.owner("member.services")).data.services.length).toBe(1);
  // The page's registry and the source it loads from hold no member's Worker.
  expect((await rig.owner("service.list")).data.services.map((s) => s.worker)).not.toContain(W);
  expect((await rig.owner("getSource?worker=" + W)).status).toBe(404);
  expect((await rig.as(A)("member.whoami")).data).toMatchObject({ did: A, methods: "com.lopecode.brain.m." + (await sha256(A)).slice(0, 10) + ".", quota: { calls: 2000, workers: 3 } });
  expect((await rig.anonymous("member.whoami")).status).toBe(403);
  expect((await rig.deployer("service.health", { worker: W })).data).toEqual({ ok: true, hash: "m1" });
  // The switch is the owner's own session's.
  expect((await rig.as(A)("member.switch", { worker: W, off: true })).status).toBe(401);
  expect((await rig.owner("member.switch", { worker: "brain-x-echo", off: true })).status).toBe(404);
  expect((await rig.owner("member.switch", { worker: W, off: true })).data).toEqual({ worker: W, off: true });
  expect((await rig.as(A)(list)).data.message).toBe(W + " is switched off");
  expect((await rig.todo(list)).status).toBe(403);
  await rig.owner("member.switch", { worker: W, off: false });
  expect((await rig.as(A)(list)).status).toBe(200);
  // Calls in and out are counted against the author's day.
  await rig.sync([{ did: A, methods: [], quota: { calls: 0 } }, { did: B, methods: [] }]);
  expect([(await rig.as(B)(list)).status, (await rig.todo(list)).status]).toEqual([429, 429]);
}
// %%
// originRig with one more Worker, brain-x-shop, whose methods have prices. `shop` is every call that reached it.
priceRig = async (config = {}) => {
  const rig = await originRig(config);
  const P = "com.lopecode.brain.", shop = [];
  rig.sim.env.X_SHOP = {
    fetch: async (request) => {
      const url = new URL(request.url), q = url.searchParams;
      if (url.pathname.endsWith("getInfo")) return Response.json({ name: "brain-x-shop", hash: "h", calls: [] });
      shop.push({ method: url.pathname.split(".").pop(), caller: request.headers.get("x-brain-caller"), origin: request.headers.get("x-brain-origin") });
      if (q.get("throw")) throw new Error("the shop fell over");
      return Response.json({ ok: true }, { status: Number(q.get("status")) || 200, headers: q.has("cost") ? { "x-brain-cost": q.get("cost") } : {} });
    }
  };
  const m = (price, more = {}) => ({ type: "procedure", allow: "true", ...(price ? { price } : {}), ...more });
  await rig.deployer("service.register", {
    worker: "brain-x-shop", role: "recipe", paths: [], secrets: [], hash: "h", keyHash: await sha256("shop-key"),
    methods: { [P + "shop.buy"]: m("0.01"), [P + "shop.big"]: m("0.03"), [P + "shop.time"]: m("double(request.params.seconds) * 0.000025"), [P + "shop.free"]: m(null), [P + "shop.text"]: m('"a lot"'), [P + "shop.less"]: m("-0.01"), [P + "shop.nan"]: m("0.0 / 0.0"), [P + "shop.dear"]: m("2.0"), [P + "shop.whole"]: m("1"), [P + "shop.nil"]: m("0.0") }
  });
  const day = (who, as = rig.owner) => as("quota.get" + (who ? "?who=" + encodeURIComponent(who) : "")).then((r) => r.data);
  const spends = () => [...rig.sim.rows.keys()].filter((k) => k.startsWith("spend/"));
  return { ...rig, shop, day, spends, today: new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10) };
}
// %%
test_a_call_with_no_price_writes_nothing = {
  const rig = await priceRig();
  // The first call a core forwards makes the key that signs origins. After that a free call writes no row.
  await rig.owner("shop.free", {});
  const before = rig.sim.rows.size;
  const r = await rig.owner("shop.free", {});
  expect([r.status, r.headers.get("x-brain-price")]).toEqual([200, null]);
  // A price of 0 is a free call as well.
  expect([(await rig.owner("shop.nil", {})).status, (await rig.anonymous("shop.nil", {})).status]).toEqual([200, 200]);
  expect([rig.sim.rows.size, rig.spends()]).toEqual([before, []]);
  return "no row written";
}
// %%
test_a_priced_call_is_charged_to_the_day_of_its_origin = {
  const rig = await priceRig();
  const r = await rig.owner("shop.buy", {});
  expect([r.status, r.headers.get("x-brain-price")]).toEqual([200, "0.01"]);
  // The price reads the request: 40 seconds at $0.000025 a second.
  expect((await rig.owner("shop.time?seconds=40", {})).headers.get("x-brain-price")).toBe("0.001");
  // $1 is the whole allowance and $0.011 of it is spent: refused.
  expect((await rig.owner("shop.whole", {})).status).toBe(402);
  expect(await rig.day()).toMatchObject({ who: "owner", day: rig.today, spent: 0.011, daily: 1, remaining: 0.989 });
  expect(rig.spends()).toEqual([`spend/${rig.today}/owner`]);
  const ledger = (await rig.owner("quota.ledger")).data;
  expect(ledger.charges.map((e) => [e.method.split(".").pop(), e.price, e.cost, e.counted, e.caller, e.origin]).reverse()).toEqual([["buy", 0.01, 0.01, true, "owner", "owner (session)"], ["time", 0.001, 0.001, true, "owner", "owner (session)"]]);
  expect([ledger.total, ledger.byWho, ledger.byMethod.length]).toEqual([0.011, [{ who: "owner", cost: 0.011 }], 2]);
  return "$" + ledger.total;
}
// %%
test_a_price_that_cannot_be_decided_refuses_the_call = {
  const rig = await priceRig();
  const tried = [];
  for (const [m, status, error] of [["text", 403, "Forbidden"], ["less", 403, "Forbidden"], ["nan", 403, "Forbidden"], ["time", 403, "Forbidden"], ["time?seconds=soon", 403, "Forbidden"], ["dear", 402, "PriceOverCeiling"]]) {
    const r = await rig.owner("shop." + m, {});
    tried.push([m, r.status, r.data.error]);
    expect([m, r.status, r.data.error]).toEqual([m, status, error]);
  }
  expect((await rig.owner("shop.less", {})).data.message).toBe("the price of com.lopecode.brain.shop.less could not be decided: it is less than 0");
  expect((await rig.owner("shop.dear", {})).data.message).toBe("com.lopecode.brain.shop.dear costs $2 for this call. The most one call may cost is $1");
  // Nothing reached the Worker and nothing was charged.
  expect([rig.shop, rig.spends()]).toEqual([[], []]);
  return tried.length + " refused";
}
// %%
test_the_origin_pays_through_one_worker_and_through_two = {
  const rig = await priceRig();
  const P = "com.lopecode.brain.";
  const spent = async () => Object.fromEntries((await rig.owner("quota.list")).data.accounts.map((a) => [a.who, a.spent]));
  // The owner's tab and the owner's turn are one account.
  await rig.owner("shop.buy", {});
  await rig.as("owner", "turn:7")("shop.buy", {});
  expect(await spent()).toEqual({ owner: 0.02 });
  // A member, a token and a Worker by its own clock each have their own.
  await rig.as("did:plc:ada", "turn:9")("shop.buy", {});
  await rig.as("token:cron", "token")("shop.buy", {});
  expect((await rig.from("a")("shop.buy", {})).status).toBe(200);
  expect(await spent()).toEqual({ "did:plc:ada": 0.01, owner: 0.02, "token:cron": 0.01, "worker:brain-x-a": 0.01 });
  // Through one Worker: a answers the member and calls the shop. The member pays, not a.
  expect((await rig.chain(rig.as("did:plc:ada", "session"), "shop.buy")).status).toBe(200);
  expect(rig.shop.at(-1)).toEqual({ method: "buy", caller: "worker:brain-x-a", origin: "did:plc:ada" });
  // Through two: a calls b for the owner, and b calls the shop.
  await rig.deployer("service.register", { worker: "brain-x-b", role: "recipe", methods: { [P + "b.go"]: { type: "procedure", who: "workers" } }, paths: [], secrets: [], hash: "h", keyHash: await sha256("b-key") });
  await rig.chain(rig.owner, "b.go");
  expect((await rig.from("b", rig.last("b").context)("shop.buy", {})).status).toBe(200);
  expect(rig.shop.at(-1)).toEqual({ method: "buy", caller: "worker:brain-x-b", origin: "owner" });
  expect(await spent()).toEqual({ "did:plc:ada": 0.02, owner: 0.03, "token:cron": 0.01, "worker:brain-x-a": 0.01 });
  // Nobody is no account: refused before the Worker, alone or through a Worker that answers them.
  const before = rig.shop.length;
  const none = await rig.anonymous("shop.buy", {});
  expect([none.status, none.data]).toEqual([402, { error: "OutOfCredits", message: "com.lopecode.brain.shop.buy costs $0.01 and anonymous has no credits" }]);
  expect((await rig.chain(rig.anonymous, "shop.buy")).status).toBe(402);
  expect(rig.shop.length).toBe(before);
  const ledger = (await rig.owner("quota.ledger?who=" + encodeURIComponent("did:plc:ada"))).data;
  expect(ledger.charges.map((e) => [e.caller, e.origin])).toEqual([["worker:brain-x-a", "did:plc:ada (session)"], ["did:plc:ada", "did:plc:ada (turn:9)"]]);
  return JSON.stringify(await spent());
}
// %%
test_out_of_credits_is_402_and_nothing_is_forwarded = {
  const rig = await priceRig();
  const ada = rig.as("did:plc:ada", "session");
  // A member has $0.10 a day: three calls of $0.03 pass and the fourth does not.
  expect([(await ada("shop.big", {})).status, (await ada("shop.big", {})).status, (await ada("shop.big", {})).status]).toEqual([200, 200, 200]);
  const no = await ada("shop.big", {});
  expect([no.status, no.data.error]).toEqual([402, "OutOfCredits"]);
  expect(no.data.message).toMatch(/^com\.lopecode\.brain\.shop\.big costs \$0\.03\. did:plc:ada has spent \$0\.09 of \$0\.1 today\. The allowance is new at 00:00 UTC, in \d+ minutes$/);
  expect(rig.shop.length).toBe(3);
  // What is left still buys what it covers.
  expect((await ada("shop.buy", {})).status).toBe(200);
  expect(await rig.day(null, ada)).toMatchObject({ who: "did:plc:ada", spent: 0.1, daily: 0.1, remaining: 0 });
  // Another account is not touched, and a free call is never refused.
  expect([(await rig.owner("shop.big", {})).status, (await ada("shop.free", {})).status]).toEqual([200, 200]);
  // The owner gives more, and the next call passes.
  expect((await rig.owner("quota.put", { who: "did:plc:ada", daily: 0.2 })).data).toMatchObject({ who: "did:plc:ada", spent: 0.1, daily: 0.2, remaining: 0.1 });
  expect((await ada("shop.big", {})).status).toBe(200);
  // A refused call counts for nothing, also after the allowance grew.
  expect((await rig.day("did:plc:ada")).spent).toBe(0.13);
  // Back to the default: null.
  expect((await rig.owner("quota.put", { who: "did:plc:ada", daily: null })).data.daily).toBe(0.1);
  expect((await ada("shop.buy", {})).status).toBe(402);
  return "402 after $0.09 of $0.10";
}
// %%
test_a_call_that_fails_is_given_back = {
  const rig = await priceRig();
  for (const q of ["status=500", "status=400", "status=302", "throw=1"]) {
    const r = await rig.owner("shop.buy?" + q, {});
    expect([q, r.status >= 300, r.headers.get("x-brain-price")]).toEqual([q, true, q === "throw=1" ? null : "0"]);
  }
  expect((await rig.day()).spent).toBe(0);
  expect((await rig.owner("shop.buy", {})).headers.get("x-brain-price")).toBe("0.01");
  const ledger = (await rig.owner("quota.ledger")).data;
  expect(ledger.charges.map((e) => [e.price, e.cost, e.refunded])).toEqual([[0.01, 0.01, false], [0.01, 0, true], [0.01, 0, true], [0.01, 0, true], [0.01, 0, true]]);
  expect(ledger.total).toBe(0.01);
  return "4 given back";
}
// %%
test_a_worker_can_say_a_call_cost_less_and_never_more = {
  const rig = await priceRig();
  const price = async (cost) => (await rig.owner("shop.big?cost=" + encodeURIComponent(cost), {})).headers.get("x-brain-price");
  // Less: the difference is given back. Nothing: all of it.
  expect([await price("0.004"), await price("0")]).toEqual(["0.004", "0"]);
  expect((await rig.day()).spent).toBe(0.004);
  // More, less than nothing, or not an amount: the price stands.
  for (const said of ["0.5", "-1", "free", "", "NaN", "0.03"]) expect([said, await price(said)]).toEqual([said, "0.03"]);
  expect((await rig.day()).spent).toBe(0.184);
  const ledger = (await rig.owner("quota.ledger")).data;
  expect(ledger.charges.slice(-2).map((e) => [e.price, e.cost, e.change])).toEqual([[0.03, 0, "settle"], [0.03, 0.004, "settle"]]);
  return "settled down twice, never up";
}
// %%
test_calls_made_at_once_do_not_spend_past_the_allowance = {
  const rig = await priceRig();
  // $1.00 a day and $0.03 a call: 33 pass, whatever the order.
  const out = await Promise.all(Array.from({ length: 50 }, () => rig.owner("shop.big", {})));
  const count = (status) => out.filter((r) => r.status === status).length;
  expect([count(200), count(402), rig.shop.length]).toEqual([33, 17, 33]);
  expect((await rig.day()).spent).toBe(0.99);
  // Calls that fail at once give back exactly what they took.
  const ada = rig.as("did:plc:ada", "session");
  const mixed = await Promise.all(Array.from({ length: 30 }, (_, i) => ada("shop.buy" + (i % 2 ? "?status=500" : ""), {})));
  expect(mixed.filter((r) => r.status === 200).length).toBeLessThanOrEqual(10);
  const spent = (await rig.day("did:plc:ada")).spent;
  expect(spent).toBe(Number((mixed.filter((r) => r.status === 200).length * 0.01).toFixed(6)));
  expect(spent).toBeLessThanOrEqual(0.1);
  return `33 of 50, then ${spent} of 0.1`;
}
// %%
test_a_new_day_starts_at_nothing_and_old_days_are_dropped = {
  const rig = await priceRig();
  const ago = (d) => new Date(Date.now() - d * 86400000).toISOString().slice(0, 10);
  const full = [{ t: 1, i: "x", u: 1000000, A: 1000000, m: "m", c: "owner", o: "owner", v: "session" }];
  for (const d of [1, 10, 31, 37]) rig.sim.rows.set(`spend/${ago(d)}/owner`, full);
  expect((await rig.owner("quota.ledger?day=" + ago(1))).data.total).toBe(1);
  // Yesterday was spent to the last cent; today is new.
  expect(await rig.day()).toMatchObject({ day: rig.today, spent: 0, remaining: 1 });
  expect((await rig.owner("shop.buy", {})).status).toBe(200);
  await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 20));
  // 30 days are kept.
  expect(rig.spends().sort()).toEqual([`spend/${ago(10)}/owner`, `spend/${ago(1)}/owner`, `spend/${rig.today}/owner`].sort());
  expect((await rig.owner("quota.ledger?day=yesterday")).status).toBe(400);
  return "a day is a row";
}
// %%
test_the_owner_sets_prices_and_allowances_in_their_own_session = {
  const rig = await priceRig();
  const P = "com.lopecode.brain.";
  const turn = rig.as("owner", "turn:7"), ada = rig.as("did:plc:ada", "session");
  // A turn, a token, a member and a Worker change nothing.
  for (const as of [turn, rig.as("token:cron", "token"), ada, rig.from("a"), rig.anonymous])
    for (const [m, body] of [["price.put", { target: P + "shop.free", price: "0.5" }], ["price.delete", { target: P + "shop.buy" }], ["quota.put", { who: "owner", daily: 100 }], ["quota.setDefaults", { member: 100 }]])
      expect([m, (await as(m, body)).status]).toEqual([m, 401]);
  expect((await rig.owner("price.list")).data.prices.find((p) => p.target === P + "shop.buy")).toEqual({ target: P + "shop.buy", worker: "brain-x-shop", declared: "0.01", set: null, setAt: null });
  // The owner's price stands in for the declared one, on a method that had none too.
  expect((await rig.owner("price.put", { target: P + "shop.buy", price: "0.02" })).data).toEqual({ target: P + "shop.buy", price: "0.02" });
  expect((await rig.owner("price.put", { method: P + "shop.free", price: 'origin.kind == "owner" ? 0.0 : 0.05' })).status).toBe(200);
  expect((await rig.owner("shop.buy", {})).headers.get("x-brain-price")).toBe("0.02");
  expect([(await rig.owner("shop.free", {})).headers.get("x-brain-price"), (await ada("shop.free", {})).headers.get("x-brain-price")]).toEqual([null, "0.05"]);
  expect((await rig.owner("price.list")).data.prices.map((p) => [p.target.split(".").pop(), p.declared, p.set]).filter((p) => p[2])).toEqual([["buy", "0.01", "0.02"], ["free", null, 'origin.kind == "owner" ? 0.0 : 0.05']]);
  // Deleted: the declared price again.
  expect((await rig.owner("price.delete", { target: P + "shop.buy" })).data).toEqual({ deleted: true });
  expect((await rig.owner("shop.buy", {})).headers.get("x-brain-price")).toBe("0.01");
  // Not a price, or not a method anyone declared.
  expect([(await rig.owner("price.put", { target: P + "shop.buy", price: "0.01 *" })).status, (await rig.owner("price.put", { target: P + "no.such", price: "0.01" })).status, (await rig.owner("price.put", { target: P + "shop.buy" })).status]).toEqual([400, 404, 400]);
  // Allowances: one account, or the defaults for a kind of account.
  expect([(await rig.owner("quota.put", { who: "everyone", daily: 1 })).status, (await rig.owner("quota.put", { who: "owner", daily: -1 })).status, (await rig.owner("quota.setDefaults", { keepDays: 0 })).status]).toEqual([400, 400, 400]);
  expect((await rig.owner("quota.setDefaults", { member: 0.5, perCall: 0.015 })).data.defaults).toEqual({ owner: 1, member: 0.5, worker: 0.1, token: 0.1, perCall: 0.015, keepDays: 30 });
  expect([(await rig.day(null, ada)).daily, (await rig.owner("shop.big", {})).data.error]).toEqual([0.5, "PriceOverCeiling"]);
  expect((await rig.owner("quota.setDefaults", { member: null, perCall: null })).data.defaults).toMatchObject({ member: 0.1, perCall: 1 });
  // An account reads its own day; only the owner reads another's, the list and the ledger.
  expect((await rig.day(null, ada)).who).toBe("did:plc:ada");
  expect([(await ada("quota.get?who=owner")).status, (await rig.anonymous("quota.get")).status, (await rig.anonymous("quota.list")).status, (await rig.anonymous("quota.ledger")).status, (await rig.anonymous("price.list")).status]).toEqual([401, 401, 401, 401, 401]);
  expect((await turn("quota.get")).data.who).toBe("owner");
  expect((await rig.owner("quota.list")).data).toMatchObject({ day: rig.today, unit: "USD", accounts: [{ who: "did:plc:ada", daily: 0.1, set: false, spent: 0.05, charges: 1 }, { who: "owner", daily: 1, set: false, spent: 0.03, charges: 2 }] });
  return "owner session only";
}
// %%
test_a_members_worker_spends_its_authors_credits = {
  const rig = await memberCoreRig(), { A, W } = rig;
  rig.sim.env.X_B = { fetch: rig.hear("b") };
  const P = "com.lopecode.brain.";
  await rig.deployer("service.register", { worker: "brain-x-b", role: "recipe", methods: { [P + "b.who"]: { type: "procedure", who: "owner", price: "0.04" } }, paths: [], secrets: [], hash: "h", keyHash: await sha256("b-key") });
  await rig.sync([{ did: A, methods: [P + "b.who"] }]);
  const todo = rig.send("https://core.internal", { "x-brain-key": "todo-key" });
  expect([(await todo("b.who", {})).status, (await todo("b.who", {})).status, (await todo("b.who", {})).status]).toEqual([200, 200, 402]);
  const day = (await rig.owner("quota.list")).data.accounts;
  expect(day.map((a) => [a.who, a.spent])).toEqual([[A, 0.08], ["owner", 0]]);
  expect((await rig.owner("quota.ledger")).data.charges[0]).toMatchObject({ who: A, caller: A, origin: `${A} (worker:${W})`, counted: true });
  return "the author pays";
}
